61856","issn":["20770383"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Clinical Medicine","paperid":"1856","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Medicine","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001327009"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7e80ab83-5856-40fd-835e-ea8e73f36a15"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Advances in Extracellular Matrix-Associated Diagnostics and Therapeutics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799851","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"I denne udgave af Didaktisk, praktisk, go’ handler det om, hvordan man som skole kan arbejde systematisk med at styrke den inkluderende praksis – med udgangspunkt i ledelse tæt på, fælles strukturer og samarbejde på tværs af faggrupper. Valdemarskolen i Ringsted har i samarbejde med Professionshøjskolen Absalon igangsat en ambitiøs kompetenceudviklingsindsats, hvor co-teaching, ressourceorienteret børnesyn og fælles referencerammer er i fokus. Hør hvordan skolen har arbejdet med analyser, teamkontrakter, handleplaner og ressourceteams – og hvordan det påvirker både børn, lærere og pædagoger i hverdagen. I studiet er skoleleder Nicholas Hansen fra Valdemarskolen sammen med Trine Skov Jensen, der til daglig arbejder med efter- og videreuddannelse i Absalons Center for Skole og Læring. Samtalen bliver styret af Lisbet Rask, som også er en del af centeret – og som til dagligt arbejder med kompetenceudvikling på skoleområdet.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rask, Lisbet","Jensen, Trine Skov","Hansen, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820718"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Børnesyn","Co teaching","Folkeskolen"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Valdemarskolen"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sammen om børnene co teaching og kulturskifte på valdemarskolen didaktisk praktisk go","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://phabsalon.dk/viden-og-inspiration/absalons-podcasts/didaktisk-praktisk-go","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-820718","ids":["pha-f1017339-deac-4e5b-a83a-47ad4f220139"],"keyword":["Børnesyn","Co-teaching","Kulturskifte","folkeskolen"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-005FC5F34B6A7EBD3928BC22EFB4529F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://phabsalon.dk/viden-og-inspiration/absalons-podcasts/didaktisk-praktisk-go","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Center for Skole og Læring - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Valdemarskolen"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbet","key":"raskoth","last":"Rask","locid":"412562a5-2a5f-4bdc-9d66-08846899e651","name":"Rask, Lisbet","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Skov","key":"jensenoth","last":"Jensen","locid":"38ccdb77-888f-4466-a371-4cd3939cd088","name":"Jensen, Trine Skov","rank":2,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"hansenoth","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Professionshøjskolen Absalon","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-f1017339-deac-4e5b-a83a-47ad4f220139"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Sammen om børnene – co-teaching og kulturskifte på Valdemarskolen : Didaktisk, praktisk, go´","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820718","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Polymeric membranes offer an appealing solution for sustainable CO2 capture, with potential for large-scale deployment. However, balancing high permeability and selectivity is an inherent challenge for pristine membranes. To address this challenge, the development of mixed matrix membranes (MMMs) is a promising strategy. MMMs are obtained by carefully integrating porous nanofillers into polymeric matrices, enabling the simultaneous enhancement of selectivity and permeability. In particular, metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) have gained recognition as MMM fillers for CO2 capture. Here, a review of the current state, recent advancements, and challenges in the fabrication and engineering of MMMs with MOFs for selective CO2 capture is proposed. Key considerations and promising research directions to fully exploit the gas separation potential of MOF-based MMMs in CO2 capture applications are highlighted.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Charlotte Skjold Qvist","Hansen, Nicholas","Motadayen, Mahboubeh","Lock, Nina","Henriksen, Martin Lahn","Quinson, Jonathan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-796388"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Quinson, Jonathan"],"keyword":["CO capture","Gas separation","Metal organic framework MOF","Mixed matrix membrane MMM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a review of metal organic frameworks and polymers in mixed matrix membranes for co sub 000000000002 sub capture","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3762/bjnano.16.14","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-796388","identifier":[{"id":"39968168","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85217719681","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11833178","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-6f35712b-57c7-4946-9a65-6f287e410f83"],"keyword":["CO capture","gas separation","inorganic filler","metal-organic framework (MOF)","mixed matrix membrane (MMM)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1540377BF22C83CD7216D58197D53171"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3762/bjnano.16.14","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering - Environmental Engineering - Ole Worms Allé 3"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Skjold Qvist","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"958b87f4-b0fd-4c46-8eb6-3999f14a456a","name":"Christensen, Charlotte Skjold Qvist","orcid":"0009-0000-1784-7070","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahboubeh","key":"motadayenpau","last":"Motadayen","locid":"79723021-76df-4f29-8d57-f90eb81d2854","name":"Motadayen, Mahboubeh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nina","key":"lockpau","last":"Lock","locid":"9838ba8c-e70d-4386-a294-94a7d7b1b2ac","name":"Lock, Nina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Lahn","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"25cf5b38-ed1a-45cf-8375-fb19db3eb73f","name":"Henriksen, Martin Lahn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonathan","key":"quinsonpau","last":"Quinson","locid":"4a006cd0-2516-4132-91ef-62f974cafab7","name":"Quinson, Jonathan","orcid":"0000-0002-9374-9330","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39968168"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3762/bjnano.16.14","issn":["21904286"],"journal":"Beilstein Journal of Nanotechnology","pages":"155-186","publisher":"Beilstein-Institut Zur Forderung der Chemischen Wissenschaften","status":"p","title":"Beilstein Journal of Nanotechnology","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217719681"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6f35712b-57c7-4946-9a65-6f287e410f83"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A review of metal-organic frameworks and polymers in mixed matrix membranes for CO<sub>2</sub> capture","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-796388","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Autonomous vessel navigation plays a vital role in enhancing maritime safety and operational efficiency, particularly in congested and complex waterways. Navigators should always display “good seamanship”. This requires the ability to predict the future evolution of scenarios, assess risks, and plan several steps ahead. However, quantifying good seamanship remains challenging due to the limited ship maneuverability, multi-vessel encounters and near ground scenario. We have developed a framework for quantifying the good seamanship score based on the collision and grounding risk that takes into account the vessel kinodynamics constraint and the uncertainty of target vessel speed. This framework helps evaluate seafarers' actions in avoiding collisions and groundings. Utilizing a quantified measure, a riskaware trajectory planning algorithm has been developed, which uses sampling-based methods to produce a safe and efficient trajectory, which is tested in various scenarios. Future efforts will address hydrodynamic effects such as wind and waves, consider target vessel future action, and explore advanced machine learning techniques to further improve the computation speed in scoring the good seamanship and generating the trajectory in complex scenario. Research Questions: - How can we define and quantify a reliable risk or good seamanship metric that accounts for all situations, including uncertainties, maneuverability limitations, different mission and vessel types, and hydrodynamic effects? - Given these factors, how can we develop a real-time algorithm that generates the optimal trajectory for an autonomous vessel?","author_count":4,"contributors":["Prabowo, Yaqub Aris","Hansen, Nicholas","Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","Galeazzi, Roberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798194"],"event":{"end":"2025-01-31","place":"Kgs. Lyngby, dk","start":"2025-01-30","title":"The 25<sup>th</sup> DNV Nordic Maritime Universities Workshop","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantifying good seamanship a framework for risk aware trajectory planning in autonomous vessel navigation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-798194","ids":["dtu-9007afbe-e360-44e8-97f1-1717d333974d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-22AC12F2FB3B96C4509313DA37BF450D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yaqub A.","key":"prabowopau","last":"Prabowo","locid":"dfe9d597-7087-43ed-b1e9-6041fbe64dc4","name":"Prabowo, Yaqub Aris","name_org":"Prabowo, Yaqub A.","orcid":"0000-0002-2500-154X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter N.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d79b2754-2197-48d4-bc85-9c4578cf9fb3","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","name_org":"Hansen, Peter N.","orcid":"0000-0001-9972-1649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dimitrios","key":"papageorgioupau","last":"Papageorgiou","locid":"1731579d-4271-42df-864e-6013a9ce795c","name":"Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","orcid":"0000-0002-4900-4083","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Roberto","key":"galeazzipau","last":"Galeazzi","locid":"b66b869e-5eed-4d7a-bc66-7f5bc41d96f7","name":"Galeazzi, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0002-6047-7922","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9007afbe-e360-44e8-97f1-1717d333974d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Quantifying Good Seamanship: A Framework for Risk- Aware Trajectory Planning in Autonomous Vessel Navigation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798194","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The extracellular matrix (ECM) protein Beta-Ig H3 (βigH3, also known as transforming growth factor β induced protein (TGFBI)) is related to poor prognosis in patients with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC). Proteolytic cleavage of βigH3 has been shown to result in release of the N-terminal fragment covering amino acid 1 to 137, but whether the degradation of βigH3 is associated to prognosis has yet to be determined. In this study we developed an ELISA targeting a collagenase generated fragment of βigH3 (cβigH3) in human serum to use the fragment as a biomarker reflecting degradation of βigH3. We demonstrated that the assay was specific to the cleaved fragment (cβigH3) and confirmed the generation of cβigH3 from degradation of fibroblast generated matrices. Moreover, higher levels of cβigH3 were released upon degradation of matrices produced by TGF-β stimulated pancreatic fibroblast compared to matrices produced by pancreatic fibroblast without TGF-β stimulation, indicating an association of the biomarker with degradation of fibrotic matrix. To evaluate the clinical relevance, we first measured cβigH3 in a cohort of 220 patients with different types of cancer with detectable levels for all 11 cancer types. We then measured the cβigH3 biomarker in pre-treatment serum from a cohort of 469 patients with locally advanced or metastatic PDAC and found that high levels of cβigH3 were associated with longer overall survival independently of age, disease stage, performance status, carbohydrate antigen 19–9 (CA19-9), and the tumor fibrosis biomarker PRO-C3 as compared to patients with high levels of cβigH3 (HR 0.78, 95% CI: 0.0.61–0.98, p = 0.04). In conclusion, cβigH3 reflects proteolytic degradation of βigH3 and shows potential as an independent prognostic biomarker for patients with advanced PDAC.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Pedersen, Rasmus S.","Hettich, Annika","Thorlacius-Ussing, Jeppe","Langholm, Lasse L.","Crespo-Bravo, Marina","Chen, Inna M.","Hansen, Carsten P.","Johansen, Julia S.","Diab, Hadi M.H.","Jorgensen, Lars N.","Karsdal, Morten","Willumsen, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818930"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteolytic degradation of beta ig h000000000003 βigh000000000003 tgfbi can be quantified non invasively in serum and predicts prognosis in patients with advanced pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-025-14283-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818930","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12093888","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40394523","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005548334","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3f1d4bc1-614d-4462-b81f-26cec646a756"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D6E492D0092634B5DCA6D8E2EC3A8E83"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-025-14283-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451409336/s12885-025-14283-w.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Graduate School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Rasmus S.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"adce4ab6-2951-4ae6-96c1-aad6ea40ec89","name":"Pedersen, Rasmus S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Annika","key":"hettichpau","last":"Hettich","locid":"079e072b-46d1-4c28-bc90-86bfaf2e22de","name":"Hettich, Annika","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jeppe","key":"thorlaciusussingpau","last":"Thorlacius-Ussing","name":"Thorlacius-Ussing, Jeppe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lasse L.","key":"langholmpau","last":"Langholm","name":"Langholm, Lasse L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marina","key":"crespobravopau","last":"Crespo-Bravo","locid":"dfef571f-413f-4473-ba49-bc65bb8cde60","name":"Crespo-Bravo, Marina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Inna M.","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Inna M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten P.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Carsten P.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Julia S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hadi M.H.","key":"diabpau","last":"Diab","name":"Diab, Hadi M.H.","rank":9,"rolecode":