{"abstract":"We report on the successful test of a new replicate drilling system for ice cores. The test was done in drill fluid, at 140 m depth in the East Greenland Ice Core Project (EastGRIP) borehole in central Greenland. A groove is first cut on the uphill side of the borehole wall using a broaching process. This groove is then used to guide a milling tool to produce a circular notch and ledge in the downhill side of the borehole. Gravity would now guide the ice core drill into this newly formed notch diverging from the parent borehole, gradually producing full-diameter replicate ice cores.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Westhoff, Julien","Boeckmann, Grant Vernon","Rathmann, Nicholas M.","Hansen, Steffen Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829196"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brief communication the danish replicate drilling system results from the first field test","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-19-3623-2025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829196","identifier":[{"id":"001567462400001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-797455f6-66de-4d09-baa0-19eee325e7d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-34F1181F0DF64D58B4AA16E193A99E4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/472933646/tc-19-3623-2025.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-19-3623-2025","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Julien","key":"westhoffpau","last":"Westhoff","locid":"604f5acb-048a-4d72-8a56-19dcf82e504a","name":"Westhoff, Julien","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Grant Vernon","key":"boeckmannpau","last":"Boeckmann","locid":"eb7434ea-97eb-466e-93c6-c42035dd5079","name":"Boeckmann, Grant Vernon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicholas Mossor","key":"rathmannpau","last":"Rathmann","locid":"3c385f2a-aa71-4f46-a0de-f5420f414fed","name":"Rathmann, Nicholas M.","name_org":"Rathmann, Nicholas Mossor","orcid":"0000-0001-7140-0931","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Steffen Bo","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8ce07904-5629-4bb2-870d-9f1692cc3007","name":"Hansen, Steffen Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/tc-19-3623-2025","issn":["19940416","19940424"],"issn_org":["19940416"],"issue":"9","journal":"Cryosphere","pages":"3623-3630","status":"p","title":"Cryosphere","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-797455f6-66de-4d09-baa0-19eee325e7d9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Brief communication : The Danish replicate drilling system - results from the first field test","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829196","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The Warburg effect, which describes the fermentation of glucose to lactate even in the presence of oxygen, is ubiquitous in proliferative mammalian cells, including cancer cells, but poses challenges for biopharmaceutical production as lactate accumulation inhibits cell growth and protein production. Previous efforts to eliminate lactate production in cells for bioprocessing have failed as lactate dehydrogenase is essential for cell growth. Here, we effectively eliminate lactate production in Chinese hamster ovary and in the human embryonic kidney cell line HEK293 by simultaneous knockout of lactate dehydrogenases and pyruvate dehydrogenase kinases, thereby removing a negative feedback loop that typically inhibits pyruvate conversion to acetyl-CoA. These cells, which we refer to as Warburg-null cells, maintain wild-type growth rates while producing negligible lactate, show a compensatory increase in oxygen consumption, near total reliance on oxidative metabolism, and higher cell densities in fed-batch cell culture. Warburg-null cells remain amenable for production of diverse biotherapeutic proteins, reaching industrially relevant titres and maintaining product glycosylation. The ability to eliminate lactate production may be useful for biotherapeutic production and provides a tool for investigating a common metabolic phenomenon.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Hefzi, Hooman","Martínez-Monge, Iván","Marín de Mas, Igor","Cowie, Nicholas Luke","Toledo, Alejandro Gomez","Noh, Soo Min","Karottki, Karen Julie la Cour","Decker, Marianne","Arnsdorf, Johnny","Camacho-Zaragoza, Jose Manuel","Kol, Stefan","Schoffelen, Sanne","Pristovšek, Nuša","Hansen, Anders Holmgaard","Miguez, Antonio A.","Petersen Bjørn, Sara","Brøndum, Karen Kathrine","Javidi, Elham Maria","Lund Jensen, Kristian","Stangl, Laura","Kreidl, Emanuel","Beuchert Kallehauge, Thomas","Ley, Daniel","Ménard, Patrice","Petersen, Helle Munck","Sukhova, Zulfiya","Bauer, Anton","Casanova, Emilio","Barron, Niall","Malmström, Johan","Nielsen, Lars K.","Min Lee, Gyun","Kildegaard, Helene Faustrup","Voldborg, Bjørn Gunnar","Lewis, Nathan E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798329"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hefzi, Hooman","Lewis, Nathan E."],"country":["Austria","Ireland","South Korea","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dublin City University","Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology","Lund University","Medical University of Vienna","National Institute for Bioprocessing Research and Training"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiplex genome editing eliminates lactate production without impacting growth rate in mammalian cells","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85217518106","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798329","identifier":[{"id":"39809975","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12272911","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85217518106","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c14c0655-7eef-4331-a9a9-fb44dd376e02"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78FFA80EAD5416DA6005A64C35FEBEFE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Medical Biote