{"abstract":"In this paper, we propose a reduced reality [RR] concept of less-is-more that virtual reality [VR] designers can use to create technological frameworks which reduce sensory overload and allow for better concentration and focus, less stress, and novel scenarios. We question the approach taken by scholars in the field of extended reality [XR] research, where the focus is typically to design and use technology that adds sensory information to the user’s perceptual field, and we address some of the confusion related to the typical uses of the term reality. To address the latter terminological muddle, we define reality as our conscious experience of the environment, an emergent perception, and we use this definition as the basis for a discussion on the role of sound in balancing sensory information and in the construction of less cluttered and less stressful perceptual environments. We further discuss current auditory strategies that reduce and alter auditory stimuli, and we suggest potential future strategies for RR that use crossmodal design approaches, masking, and filtering techniques.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","Walther-Hansen, Mads"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-704796"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Walther-Hansen, Mads"],"keyword":["Auditory Perception","Diminished reality","Extended reality","Presence","Reduced reality","Sound"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"less is more auditory strategies for reduced reality","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00779-024-01808-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Aalborg University"],"id":"S01-000.00-704796","identifier":[{"id":"85196029268","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-125cd619-8728-47df-b090-18da28f9f47d"],"keyword":["Auditory perception","Diminished reality","Extended reality","Presence","Reduced reality","Sound"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FB2E4D22500FAA60EAD5ECB08A87CB5F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00779-024-01808-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/769157987/s00779-024-01808-6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Art, Aesthetics & Health","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music & Sound Knowledge Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Tid, Eksistens og Naturforbundethed"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark Nicholas","key":"grimshawaagaardpau","last":"Grimshaw-Aagaard","locid":"673322d2-f25b-4f45-93b2-ba1c4c9fdbc5","name":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0003-0485-6087","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"waltherhansenpau","last":"Walther-Hansen","locid":"73804945-3d74-4f54-a2db-ab1be9009c09","name":"Walther-Hansen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0001-5746-5093","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00779-024-01808-6","issn":["16174909","16174917"],"issn_org":["16174909"],"issue":"5","journal":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","pages":"713-725","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196029268"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-125cd619-8728-47df-b090-18da28f9f47d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Less-Is-More : Auditory Strategies for Reduced Reality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-704796","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This is the eighth annual summary of the International Liaison Committee on Resuscitation International Consensus on Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation and Emergency Cardiovascular Care Science With Treatment Recommendations; a more comprehensive review was done in 2020. This latest summary addresses the most recent published resuscitation evidence reviewed by the International Liaison Committee on Resuscitation task force science experts. Members from 6 International Liaison Committee on Resuscitation task forces have assessed, discussed, and debated the quality of the evidence, using Grading of Recommendations Assessment, Development, and Evaluation criteria, and their statements include consensus treatment recommendations. Insights into the deliberations of the task forces are provided in the Justification and Evidence-to-Decision Framework Highlights sections. In addition, the task forces list priority knowledge gaps for further research.","author_count":157,"contributors":["Greif, Robert","Bray, Janet E","Djärv, Therese","Drennan, Ian R","Liley, Helen G","Ng, Kee-Chong","Cheng, Adam","Douma, Matthew J","Scholefield, Barnaby R","Smyth, Michael","Weiner, Gary","Abelairas-Gómez, Cristian","Acworth, Jason","Anderson, Natalie","Atkins, Dianne L","Berry, David C","Bhanji, Farhan","Böttiger, Bernd W","Bradley, Richard N","Breckwoldt, Jan","Carlson, Jestin N","Cassan, Pascal","Chang, Wei-Tien","Charlton, Nathan P","Phil Chung, Sung","Considine, Julie","Cortegiani, Andrea","Costa-Nobre, Daniela T","Couper, Keith","Couto, Thomaz Bittencourt","Dainty, Katie N","Dassanayake, Vihara","Davis, Peter G","Dawson, Jennifer A","de Caen, Allan R","Deakin, Charles D","Debaty, Guillaume","Del Castillo, Jimena","Dewan, Maya","Dicker, Bridget","Djakow, Jana","Donoghue, Aaron J","Eastwood, Kathryn","El-Naggar, Walid","Escalante-Kanashiro, Raffo","Fabres, Jorge","Farquharson, Barbara","Fawke, Joe","de Almeida, Maria Fernanda","Fernando, Shannon M","Finan, Emer","Finn, Judith","F