{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777034"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discourse analysis post structuralism and foreign policy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://global.oup.com/academic/product/foreign-policy-9780192863072?q=Foreign%2520Policy%2520Theories%252C%2520Actors%252C%2520Cases&lang=en&cc=dk%23","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777034","ids":["ku-150dde99-7bd6-4ed5-9a59-e00444a39e5b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6EA7F5C369AD52DA140E8E695D2CEC35"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, Gender & Politics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science, International Relations"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"e20d032f-b24f-409c-8abc-0389b4d9d95e","name":"Hansen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-7918-3943","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steve","key":"smithpedh","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Steve","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Amelia","key":"hadfieldpedh","last":"Hadfield","name":"Hadfield, Amelia","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tim","key":"dunnepedh","last":"Dunne","name":"Dunne, Tim","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicholas","key":"kitchenpedh","last":"Kitchen","name":"Kitchen, Nicholas","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"4","isbn":["9780192863072"],"pages":"95-110","place":"Oxford","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Theories, Actors, Cases","title":"Foreign Policy"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-150dde99-7bd6-4ed5-9a59-e00444a39e5b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discourse analysis, post-structuralism, and foreign policy","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777034","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Genetic studies have identified numerous regions associated with plasma fibrinogen levels in Europeans, yet missing heritability and limited inclusion of non-Europeans necessitates further studies with improved power and sensitivity. Compared with array-based genotyping, whole genome sequencing (WGS) data provides better coverage of the genome and better representation of non-European variants. To better understand the genetic landscape regulating plasma fibrinogen levels, we meta-analyzed WGS data from the NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine (TOPMed) program (n=32,572), with array-based genotype data from the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology (CHARGE) Consortium (n=131,340) imputed to the TOPMed or Haplotype Reference Consortium panel. We identified 18 loci that have not been identified in prior genetic studies of fibrinogen. Of these, four are driven by common variants of small effect with reported MAF at least 10 percentage points higher in African populations. Three signals (SERPINA1, ZFP36L2, and TLR10) contain predicted deleterious missense variants. Two loci, SOCS3 and HPN, each harbor two conditionally distinct, non-coding variants. The gene region encoding the fibrinogen protein chain subunits (FGG;FGB;FGA), contains 7 distinct signals, including one novel signal driven by rs28577061, a variant common in African ancestry populations but extremely rare in Europeans (MAFAFR=0.180; MAFEUR=0.008). Through phenome-wide association studies in the VA Million Veteran Program, we found associations between fibrinogen polygenic risk scores and thrombotic and inflammatory disease phenotypes, including an association with gout. Our findings demonstrate the utility of WGS to augment genetic discovery in diverse populations and offer new insights for putative mechanisms of fibrinogen regulation.","author_count":136,"contributors":["Huffman, Jennifer E","Nicholas, Jayna","Hahn, Julie","Heath, Adam S","Raffield, Laura M","Yanek, Lisa R","Brody, Jennifer A","Thibord, Florian","Almasy, Laura","Bartz, Traci M","Bielak, Lawrence F","Bowler, Russell P","Carrasquilla, Germán D","Chasman, Daniel I","Chen, Ming-Huei","Emmert, David B","Ghanbari, Mohsen","Haessler, Jeffrey","Hottenga, Jouke J","Kleber, Marcus E","Le, Ngoc-Quynh","Lee, Jiwon","Lewis, Joshua P","Li-Gao, Ruifang","Luan, Jian'an","Malmberg, Anni Liisi","Mangino, Massimo","Marioni, Riccardo","Martinez-Perez, Angel","Pankratz, Nathan","Polasek, Ozren","Richmond, Anne","Rodriguez, Benjamin A T","Rotter, Jerome I","Steri, Maristella","Suchon, Pierre","Trompet, Stella","Weiss, Stefan","Zare, Marjan","Auer, Paul L","Cho, Michael","Christofidou, Paraskevi","Davies, Gail","de Geus, Eco Jc","Deleuze, Jean-François","Delgado, Graciela E","Ekunwe, Lynette","Faraday, Nauder","Gogele, Martin","Greinacher, Andreas","Gao, He","Howard, Tom E","Joshi, Peter K","Kilpeläinen, Tuomas O","Lahti, Jari","Linneberg, Allan","Naitza, Silvia","Noordam, Raymond","Vergés, Ferran Paüls","Rich, Stephen S","Rosendaal, Frits R","Rudan, Igor","Ryan, Kathleen A","Souto, Juan Carlos Carlos","van Rooij, Frank J A","Wang, Heming","Zhao, Wei","Becker, Lewis","Beswick, Andrew","Brown, Michael R","Cade, Brian","Campbell, Harry","Cho, Kelly","Crapo, James","Curran, Joanne","de Maat, Moniek P M","Doyle, Margaret F","Elliott, Paul","Floyd, James S","Fuchsberger, Christian","Grarup, Niels","Guo, Xiuqing","Harris, Sarah","Hou, Lifang","Kolcic, Ivana","Kooperberg, Charles","Menni, Cristina","Nauck, Matthias","O'Connell, Jeffrey R","Orru, Valeria","Psaty, Bruce M","Räikkönen, Katri","Smith, Jennifer A","Soria, Jose Manuel","Stott, David","van Hylckama Vlieg, Astrid","Watkins, Hugh","Willemsen, Gonneke","Wilson, Peter Wf","Ben-Shlomo, Yoav","Blangero, John","Boomsma, Dorret","Cox, Simon R","Dehghan, Abbas","Eriksson, Johan G","Fiorillo, Edoardo","Fornage, Myriam","Hansen, Torben","Hayward, Caroline","Ikram, Mohammad Arfan","Jukema, J Wouter","Kardia, Sharon","Lange, Leslie","Maerz, Winfried","Mathias, Rasika","Mitchell, Braxton D","Mook-Kanamori, Dennis O","Morange, Pierre-Emmanuel","Pedersen, Oluf","Pramstaller, Peter P","Redline, Susan","Reiner, Alex P","Ridker, Paul M","Silverman, Edwin K","Spector, Tim D","Volker, Uwe","Wareham, Nick","Wilson, James","Yao, Jie","Tregouet, David-Alexandre","Johnson, Andrew D","Wolberg, Alisa S","de Vries, Paul S","Sabater-Lleal, Maria","Morrison, Alanna","Smith, Nicholas L"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777573"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Finland","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille University","All Global Affiliations","American University Washington DC","Atlanta Veterans Affairs Medical Center","Boston University","Brigham and Women’s Hospital","Department of Veterans Affairs","EURAC Research","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Helsinki University Hospital","Imperial College London","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Johns Hopkins University","Karolinska Institutet","King's College London","Leiden University","Maverick Technologies","National Institutes of Health","National Jewish Health","National Research Council of Italy (CNR)","Paris-Saclay University","SYNLAB International GmbH","Stanford University","University of Bristol","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Cambridge","University of Colorado Boulder","University of Edinburgh","University of Glasgow","University of Greifswald","University of Maryland, College Park","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Oxford","University of Pennsylvania","University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Texas Rio Grande Valley","University