-7be0c2e60925"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genome-wide association analyses identify 95 risk loci and provide insights into the neurobiology of post-traumatic stress disorder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.61-741800","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Receptor-interacting serine/threonine-protein kinase 1 (RIPK1) functions as a critical stress sentinel that coordinates cell survival, inflammation, and immunogenic cell death (ICD). Although the catalytic function of RIPK1 is required to trigger cell death, its non-catalytic scaffold function mediates strong pro-survival signaling. Accordingly, cancer cells can hijack RIPK1 to block necroptosis and evade immune detection. We generated a small-molecule proteolysis-targeting chimera (PROTAC) that selectively degraded human and murine RIPK1. PROTAC-mediated depletion of RIPK1 deregulated TNFR1 and TLR3/4 signaling hubs, accentuating the output of NF-κB, MAPK, and IFN signaling. Additionally, RIPK1 degradation simultaneously promoted RIPK3 activation and necroptosis induction. We further demonstrated that RIPK1 degradation enhanced the immunostimulatory effects of radio- and immunotherapy by sensitizing cancer cells to treatment-induced TNF and interferons. This promoted ICD, antitumor immunity, and durable treatment responses. Consequently, targeting RIPK1 by PROTACs emerges as a promising approach to overcome radio- or immunotherapy resistance and enhance anticancer therapies.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Mannion, Jonathan","Gifford, Valentina","Bellenie, Benjamin","Fernando, Winnie","Ramos Garcia, Laura","Wilson, Rebecca","John, Sidonie Wicky","Udainiya, Savita","Patin, Emmanuel C.","Tiu, Crescens","Smith, Angel","Goicoechea, Maria","Craxton, Andrew","Moraes de Vasconcelos, Nathalia","Guppy, Naomi","Cheung, Kwai Ming J.","Cundy, Nicholas J.","Pierrat, Olivier","Brennan, Alfie","Roumeliotis, Theodoros I.","Benstead-Hume, Graeme","Alexander, John","Muirhead, Gareth","Layzell, Scott","Lyu, Wenxin","Roulstone, Victoria","Allen, Mark","Baldock, Holly","Legrand, Arnaud","Gabel, Florian","Serrano-Aparicio, Natalia","Starling, Chris","Guo, Hongyan","Upton, Jason","Gyrd-Hansen, Mads","MacFarlane, Marion","Seddon, Benedict","Raynaud, Florence","Roxanis, Ioannis","Harrington, Kevin","Haider, Syed","Choudhary, Jyoti S.","Hoelder, Swen","Tenev, Tencho","Meier, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749272"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Auburn University","Louisiana State University in Shreveport","The Institute of Cancer Research, London","University College London","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Cell Death","Immunotherapy","Inflammation","Interferon","Necroptosis","RIPK1","Radiotherapy","TLR3","TNF"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a ripk000000000001 specific protac degrader achieves potent antitumor activity by enhancing immunogenic cell death","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2024.04.025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749272","identifier":[{"id":"38788712","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11236506","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195286501","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-db10cb4c-1604-4a20-81cd-6453277bbf7d"],"keyword":["RIPK1","TLR3","TNF","anticancer immunity","cell death","immunotherapy","inflammation","interferon","necroptosis","radiotherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A2ACFFD205C03CBFC566E294739D4F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397992958/A_RIPK1_specific_PROTAC.htm","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2024.04.025","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"the institute of cancer research london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Institute of Cancer Research, London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Skin Immunology Research Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"louisiana state university in shreveport","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Louisiana State University in Shreveport","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"auburn university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Auburn University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonathan","key":"mannionpau","last":"Mannion","name":"Mannion, Jonathan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Valentina","key":"giffordpau","last":"Gifford","name":"Gifford, Valentina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Benjamin","key":"belleniepau","last":"Bellenie","name":"Bellenie, Benjamin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Winnie","key":"fernandopau","last":"Fernando","name":"Fernando, Winnie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laura","key":"ramosgarciapau","last":"Ramos Garcia","name":"Ramos Garcia, Laura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rebecca","key":"wilsonpau","last":"Wilson","name":"Wilson, Rebecca","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidonie 