{"abstract":"Introduction. Persister cells are transiently non-growing antibiotic-tolerant bacteria that cause infection relapse, and there is no effective antibiotic therapy to tackle these infections.Gap statement. High-throughput assays in drug discovery are biased towards detecting drugs that inhibit bacterial growth rather than killing non-growing bacteria. A new and simple assay to discover such drugs is needed.Aim. This study aims to develop a simple and high-throughput assay to identify compounds with antimicrobial activity against persister cells and use it to identify molecular motifs with such activity.Methodology. We quantified Staphylococcus aureus persister cells by enumeration of colony forming units after 24 h ciprofloxacin treatment. We first quantified how the cell concentration, antibiotic concentration, growth phase and presence/absence of nutrients during antibiotic exposure affected the fraction of persister cells in a population. After optimizing these parameters, we screened the antimicrobial activity of compound fragments to identify molecular structures that have activity against persister cells.Results. Exponential- and stationary-phase cultures transferred to nutrient-rich media displayed a bi-phasic time-kill curve and contained 0.001-0.07% persister cells. A short rifampicin treatment resulted in 100% persister cells for 7 h, after which cells resumed activity and became susceptible. Stationary-phase cultures displayed a low but constant death rate but ultimately resulted in similarly low survival rates as the exponential-phase cultures after 24 h ciprofloxacin treatment. The persister phenotype was only maintained in most of the population for 24 h if cells were transferred to a carbon-free minimal medium before exposure to ciprofloxacin. Keeping cells starved enabled the generation of high concentrations of S. aureus cells that tolerate 50× MIC ciprofloxacin, and we used this protocol for rapid screening for biocidal antibiotics. We identified seven compounds from four structural clusters with activity against antibiotic-tolerant S. aureus. Two compounds were moderately cytotoxic, and the rest were highly cytotoxic.Conclusion. Transferring a stationary-phase culture to a carbon-free minimal medium for antimicrobial testing is a simple strategy for high-throughput screening for new antibiotics that kill persister cells. We identified molecule fragments with such activity, but further screening is needed to identify motifs with lower general cytotoxicity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Petersen, Maiken Engelbrecht","Hansen, Liva Kjær","Mitkin, Alexander Alexandrovich","Kelly, Nicholas M.","Wood, Thomas Keith","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752784"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pennsylvania State University"],"keyword":["Drug development","Persister cells","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a high throughput assay identifies molecules with antimicrobial activity against persister cells","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.001856","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752784","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11316564","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38995832","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85198570761","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-41a1fd89-75c7-4eb4-afb9-3b9c78d9f62b"],"keyword":["Staphylococcus aureus","drug development","persister cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6FFA801CBD892126B1EA2B89DCAA646"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.001856","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Pincer Biotech ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"pennsylvania state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pennsylvania State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken Engelbrecht","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"99c8dbe5-12c1-4b7b-bc1d-a2985885e525","name":"Petersen, Maiken Engelbrecht","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liva Kjær","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"653924b2-77cf-4c6c-b9d3-9f1bd34da92f","name":"Hansen, Liva Kjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Alexandrovich","key":"mitkinpau","last":"Mitkin","locid":"e8d98ae8-db91-4fb5-a72f-87ba7fcced6d","name":"Mitkin, Alexander Alexandrovich","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas M.","key":"kellypau","last":"Kelly","name":"Kelly, Nicholas M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Keith","key":"woodpau","last":"Wood","name":"Wood, Thomas Keith","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis Pedersen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Jørgen","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"fb8358a6-187a-4d5f-8187-06051ed74173","name":"Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-2459-0511","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38995832"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1099/jmm.0.001856","issn":["00222615","14735644"],"issn_org":["00222615"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Medical Microbiology","paperid":"001856","publisher":"Microbiology Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Microbiology","volume":"73"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198570761"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","pincer biotech aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-41a1fd89-75c7-4eb4-afb9-3b9c78d9f62b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A high-throughput assay identifies molecules with antimicrobial activity against persister cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752784","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"GreenHopper is the first Danish zero-emission ferry developed as a test platform for autonomous waterborne navigation technologies. The paper presents technology development within the innovation project ShippingLab Autonomy, which led to the commissioning of GreenHopper at Limfjorden (DK) in December 2022. The technology research resulted in a holistic system architecture for surface vessel autonomy, based on distribution of functionality and responsibility on software modules, similar to the structure observed in the International Maritime Organization (IMO) Seafarers Training Certification and Watch-keeping (STCW) regulatory framework. The paper shows how this approach results in an architecture that supports safe behaviours of individual modules and of autonomous navigation at a system level. The paper presents the individual modules, specific features and benefits. Elements of the regulatory framework are highlighted to poise technology approval by maritime authorities. The paper reflects on lessons learned, discusses continued technology validation in dedicated operational scenarios.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Blanke, Mogens","Hansen, Nicholas","Dittmann, Kjeld","Enevoldsen, Thomas Thuesen","Dagdilelis, Dimitrios","Schöller, Frederik Emil Thorsson","Plenge-Feidenhans'l, Martin Krarup","Becktor, Jonathan Binner","Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","Galeazzi, Roberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775455"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-30","place":"Trondheim, no","start":"2024-10-29","title":"2024 International Maritime and Port Technology and Development Conference, and the 6<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Maritime Autonomous Surface Ships","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["ABB A/S, Marine and Ports"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenhopper the danish spearhead towards autonomous waterborne mobility","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1742-6596/2867/1/012035","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-775455","identifier":[{"id":"85208118339","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-64756d39-b71e-4f82-95ec-5ac31f75dad3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-41FB700AE795EB50B9DE575DC99EA660"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1742-6596/2867/1/012035","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/378235199/Blanke_2024_J._Phys._Conf._Ser._2867_012035.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["ABB A/S, Marine and Ports"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"blankepau","last":"Blanke","locid":"a4238b5e-294f-4ee2-a56d-a9f9473eb715","name":"Blanke, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-9181-9518","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk",