{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Alzheimer's disease (AD) is a neurodegenerative disease and the main cause of dementia in the elderly. AD pathology is characterized by accumulation of microglia around the beta-amyloid (Aβ) plaques which assumes disease-specific transcriptional signatures, as for the disease-associated microglia (DAM). However, the regulators of microglial phagocytosis are still unknown. METHODS: We isolated Aβ-laden microglia from the brain of 5xFAD mice for RNA sequencing to characterize the transcriptional signature in phagocytic microglia and to identify the key non-coding RNAs capable of regulating microglial phagocytosis. Through spatial sequencing, we show the transcriptional changes of microglia in the AD mouse brain in relation to Aβ proximity. RESULTS: Finally, we show that phagocytic messenger RNAs are regulated by miR-7a-5p, miR-29a-3p and miR-146a-5p microRNAs and segregate the DAM population into phagocytic and non-phagocytic states. DISCUSSION: Our study pinpoints key regulators of microglial Aβ clearing capacity suggesting new targets for future therapeutic approaches.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Scoyni, Flavia","Giudice, Luca","Väänänen, Mari Anna","Downes, Nicholas","Korhonen, Paula","Choo, Xin Yi","Välimäki, Nelli Noora","Mäkinen, Petri","Korvenlaita, Nea","Rozemuller, Annemieke J.","de Vries, Helga E.","Polo, Jose","Turunen, Tiia A.","Ylä-Herttuala, Seppo","Hansen, Thomas Birkballe","Grubman, Alexandra","Kaikkonen, Minna U.","Malm, Tarja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-727472"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Malm, Tarja","Scoyni, Flavia"],"country":["Australia","Finland","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Monash University","University of Eastern Finland","VU University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Alzheimer s disease","MicroRNAs","Microglia","Phagocytosis","Post transcriptional regulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alzheimer s disease induced phagocytic microglia express a specific profile of coding and non coding rnas","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/alz.13502","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-727472","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10916983","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37828821","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85173856636","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-606ee5df-8f52-4992-80aa-dba08ca74701"],"keyword":["Alzheimer's disease","microRNAs","microglia","phagocytosis","post-transcriptional regulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C07F8C50E534BA5ED7A292445E99A6BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/alz.13502","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of eastern finland","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Eastern Finland","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"vu university amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"VU University Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - RNA Biology and Innovation","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flavia","key":"scoynipau","last":"Scoyni","name":"Scoyni, Flavia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"giudicepau","last":"Giudice","name":"Giudice, Luca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mari Anna","key":"väänänenpau","last":"Väänänen","name":"Väänänen, Mari Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"downespau","last":"Downes","name":"Downes, Nicholas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paula","key":"korhonenpau","last":"Korhonen","name":"Korhonen, Paula","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin Yi","key":"choopau","last":"Choo","name":"Choo, Xin Yi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nelli Noora","key":"välimäkipau","last":"Välimäki","name":"Välimäki, Nelli Noora","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petri","key":"mäkinenpau","last":"Mäkinen","name":"Mäkinen, Petri","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nea","key":"korvenlaitapau","last":"Korvenlaita","name":"Korvenlaita, Nea","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Annemieke J.","key":"rozemullerpau","last":"Rozemuller","name":"Rozemuller, Annemieke J.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helga E.","key":"devriespau","last":"de Vries","name":"de Vries, Helga E.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jose","key":"polopau","last":"Polo","name":"Polo, Jose","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tiia A.","key":"turunenpau","last":"Turunen","name":"Turunen, Tiia A.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seppo","key":"yläherttualapau","last":"Ylä-Herttuala","name":"Ylä-Herttuala, Seppo","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas B.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"e00bd2ad-0f79-4307-9f42-00ae2e99e2ca","name":"Hansen, Thomas Birkballe","name_org":"Hansen, Thomas B.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandra","key":"grubmanpau","last":"Grubman","name":"Grubman, Alexandra","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Minna U.","key":"kaikkonenpau","last":"Kaikkonen","name":"Kaikkonen, Minna U.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tarja","key":"malmpau","last":"Malm","name":"Malm, Tarja","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37828821"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/alz.13502","issn":["15525260","15525279"],"issn_org":["15525260"],"issue":"2","journal":"Alzheimer's & Dementia","pages":"954-974","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Alzheimer's & Dementia","title_org":"Alzheimer's and Dementia","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173856636"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-606ee5df-8f52-4992-80aa-dba08ca74701"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Alzheimer's disease-induced phagocytic microglia express a specific profile of coding and non-coding RNAs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-727472","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Autoimmune diseases have been linked to an increased risk of pregnancy-related complications. A family history of autoimmune diseases may be related to the risk of childhood cancer based on similar histocompatibility antigens. We utilized data from national registries in Denmark to examine associations between maternal autoimmune disease and cancer in their offspring. METHODS: We linked data from several national registries in Denmark to identify childhood cancer cases in children <20 years diagnosed between 1977 to 2016. Controls were selected from the Central Population Register and matched to cases by birth year and sex (25:1). Mothers with autoimmune disease diagnosed in pregnancy or prior were identified from the National Patient Register. Multivariable conditional logistic regression analyses were used to estimate associations between maternal autoimmune diseases and childhood cancer in offspring. RESULTS: Autoimmune diseases (all types) were positively associated with all childhood cancers combined (Odds Ratio (OR) = 1.25, 95% CI 1.06, 1.47), acute lymphoblastic leukemia (OR =1.52, 95% CI 1.09, 2.13), Burkitt lymphoma (OR = 2.69, 95% CI 1.04, 6.97), and central nervous system tumors (OR = 1.45, 95% CI 1.06, 1.99), especially astrocytoma (OR = 2.27, 95% CI 1.36, 3.77) and glioma (OR = 1.75, 95% CI 1.13, 2.73). When we examined mothers with rheumatoid arthritis, we observed an increased association for all cancers (OR = 2.15, 95% CI 1.40, 3.30), acute lymphoblastic leukemia (OR = 3.55, 95% CI 1.69, 7.47), and central nervous system tumors (OR = 2.91, 95% CI 1.46, 5.82), especially glioma (OR = 3.58, 95% CI 1.40, 9.18) in offspring. CONCLUSION: There is a positive association between maternal autoimmune disease and childhood cancer. This association is especially prominent in the offspring of women with rheumatoid arthritis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Orimoloye, Helen T.","Nguyen, Nicholas","Deng, Chuanjie","Saechao, Chai","Ritz, Beate","Olsen, Jørn","Hansen, Johnni","Heck, Julia E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-737745"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Heck, Julia E."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at Los Angeles","University of North Texas"],"keyword":["Childhood cancer","Inflammatory bowel disease","Leukemia","Pregnancy","Psoriasis","Rheumatoid arthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"maternal autoimmune disease and its association with childhood cancer a population based case control study in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejcped.2024.100145","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-737745","identifier":[{"id":"85190365925","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38298419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10827341","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-cf66a031-a406-4b84-930f-b3613112cd16"],"keyword":["Childhood cancer","Inflammatory bowel disease","Leukemia","Maternal autoimmune diseases","Pregnancy","Psoriasis","Rheumatoid arthritis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E15F5B9379A8D75A42890E53054D2496"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejcped.2024.100145","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of north texas","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of North Texas","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at los angeles","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Los Angeles","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helen T.","key":"orimoloyepau","last":"Orimoloye","name":"Orimoloye, Helen T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"nguyenpau","last":"Nguyen","name":"Nguyen, Nicholas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuanjie","key":"dengpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Chuanjie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chai","key":"saechaopau","last":"Saechao","name":"Saechao, Chai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Beate","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","name":"Ritz, Beate","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jorn","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"48e09bb0-9b9d-40c8-ab2c-ff256ae11f0f","name":"Olsen, Jørn","name_org":"Olsen, Jorn","orcid":"0000-0001-7462-5140","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnni","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Johnni","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julia E.","key":"heckpau","last":"Heck","name":"Heck, Julia E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38298419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejcped.2024.100145","issn":["2772610X"],"journal":"EJC Paediatric Oncology","paperid":"100145","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"EJC Paediatric Oncology","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190365925"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cf66a031-a406-4b84-930f-b3613112cd16"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Maternal autoimmune disease and its association with childhood cancer : A population-based case-control study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-737745","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Atrial fibrillation is highly prevalent in patients on chronic dialysis. It is unclear whether anticoagulant therapy for stroke prevention is beneficial in these patients. Vitamin K-antagonists (VKA) remain the predominant anticoagulant choice. Importantly, anticoagulation remains inconsistently used and a possible benefit remains untested in randomised clinical trials comparing oral anticoagulation with no treatment in patients on chronic dialysis. The Danish Warfarin-Dialysis (DANWARD) trial aims to investigate the safety and efficacy of VKAs in patients with atrial fibrillation on chronic dialysis. The hypothesis is that VKA treatment compared with no treatment is associated with stroke risk reduction and overall benefit. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: The DANWARD trial is an investigator-initiated trial at 13 Danish dialysis centres. In an open-label randomised clinical trial study design, a total of 718 patients with atrial fibrillation on chronic dialysis will be randomised in a 1:1 ratio to receive either standard dose VKA targeting an international normalised ratio of 2.0-3.0 or no oral anticoagulation. Principal analyses will compare the risk of a primary efficacy endpoint, stroke or transient ischaemic attack and a primary safety endpoint, major bleeding, in patients allocated to VKA treatment and no treatment, respectively. The first patient was randomised in October 2019. Patients will be followed until 1 year after the inclusion of the last patient. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The study protocol was approved by the Regional Research Ethics Committee (journal number H-18050839) and the Danish Medicines Agency (case number 2018101877). The trial is conducted in accordance with the Helsinki declaration and standards of Good Clinical Practice. Study results will be disseminated to participating sites, at research conferences and in peer-reviewed journals. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBERS: NCT03862859, EUDRA-CT 2018-000484-86 and CTIS ID 2022-502500-75-00.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Ballegaard, Ellen Linnea Freese","Lindhard, Kristine","Lindhardt, Morten","Peters, Christian Daugaard","Thomsen Nielsen, Finn","Tietze, Ida Nørager","Borg, Rikke","Boesby, Lene","Bertelsen, Marianne Camilla","Brøsen, Julie Maria Bøggild","Cibulskyte-Ninkovic, Donata","Rantanen, Jesper Moesgaard","Mose, Frank Holden","Kampmann, Jan Dominik","Nielsen, Alice Skovhede","Breinholt, Johanne Kodal","Kofod, Dea Haagensen","Bressendorff, Iain","Clausen, Peter Vilhelm","Lange, Theis","Køber, Lars","Kamper, Anne-Lise","Bang, Casper Niels Furbo","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Hansen, Ditte","Grove, Erik L","Gislason, Gunnar","Jensen, Jens Dam","Olesen, Jonas Bjerring","Hornum, Mads","Rix, Marianne","Schou, Morten","Carlson, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S04-099.51-724050"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Ballegaard, Ellen Linnea Freese"],"keyword":["Anticoagulants adverse effects","Anticoagulation","Atrial Fibrillation complications","Clinical trial","Denmark","Dialysis","End stage renal failure","Humans","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Renal Dialysis","Stroke prevention control","Thromboembolism","Treatment Outcome","Warfarin therapeutic use"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for a randomised controlled trial comparing warfarin with no oral anticoagulation in patients with atrial fibrillation on chronic dialysis the danish warfarin dialysis danward trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-081961","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["CDP has received speaker honoraria or consultancy fees from AstraZeneca and Astellas. Support for attending meetings and travel from Boehringer Ingelheim. CDP also has an ongoing collaboration with Vifor Pharma including donation of a research grant unrelated to this study. DH has received speaker and consultancy fees from AstraZeneca, GlaxoSmithKline and UCB Nordic. ELFB has received a donation of a research grant from AstraZeneca unrelated to this study. ELG has received speaker honoraria or consultancy fees from AstraZeneca, Bayer, Boehringer Ingelheim, Bristol-Myers Squibb, Pfizer, Novo Nordisk, MSD, Lundbeck Pharma and Organon. He is an investigator in clinical studies sponsored by AstraZeneca, Idorsia or Bayer and has received unrestricted research grants from Boehringer Ingelheim. IB has received speaker honoraria from Amgen and Bayer. JBO has received speaker honoraria or consultancy fees from Bayer, Bristol-Myers Squibb, Organon and Pfizer. LB has received consultancy fees from AstraZeneca, Astellas, Vifor Pharma, Pfizer and Novartis. LK has received speaker honoraria from AstraZeneca, Bayer, Boehringer Ingelheim, Novartis and Novo Nordisk. MH has received speaker and consultancy fees from AstraZeneca, Bayer, Boehringer Ingelheim, Vifor and GSK within the last 3 years. ML has received speaker and consultancy fees from AstraZeneca, Bayer, Boehringer Ingelheim, Novo Nordisk and GlaxoSmithKline. NC has received speaker honoraria from AstraZeneca and Bristol-Myers Squibb. RB has received speaker honoraria or consultancy fees from AstraZeneca, Bayer and Boehringer Ingelheim. She is an investigator in clinical studies sponsored by Boehringer Ingelheim, AstraZeneca or Bayer an