{"abstract":"Automation and robotics are essential for the effective monitoring and inspection of maritime critical infrastructures and marine environments. We demonstrate the use of an unmanned surface vehicle, integrated with acoustic and optical sensors, to perform fast and accurate inspections of maritime infrastructures in confined areas (i.e., presence of buildings and multiple obstacles). High resolution maps are obtained fusing offline data from LiDAR and 2D acoustic multi-beam forward looking camera point clouds. The technological pipeline is demonstrated through a survey in Copenhagen harbour. The data acquisition leverages on methods to improve path planning and localization to correct failures in the RTK GNSS due to shadowing of buildings and other obstacles. The entire data flow is streamlined to produce fast delivery time and data access, optimizing data acquisition and processing, providing results into a dedicated web service tailored to users’ needs for knowledge and information extraction.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thompson, Fletcher","Hansen, Nicholas","Galeazzi, Roberto","Palma, Marco","Brock, Andreas Libonati","Mariani, Patrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764354"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-11","place":"Venice, it","start":"2024-07-08","title":"27<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Information Fusion","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UBICA s.r.l."],"keyword":["Infrastructure monitoring","LiDAR","Sensor fusion","Surveillance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Københavns Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomous inspection and data fusion for maritime critical infrastructures","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85207692230","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764354","identifier":[{"id":"85207692230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ab955fc5-e971-4f02-a325-003cad6eaf8b"],"keyword":["Forward looking sonar","Infrastructure monitoring","LiDAR","Sensor fusion","Surveillance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C5AA6B3E47DC52EB6382F1AF056622CE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Oceans and Arctic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"ubica s r l","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UBICA s.r.l.","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Københavns Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fletcher","key":"thompsonpau","last":"Thompson","locid":"946f542b-8850-4464-beb4-384eeab5bad7","name":"Thompson, Fletcher","orcid":"0000-0002-0639-9871","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Nicholas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d79b2754-2197-48d4-bc85-9c4578cf9fb3","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","name_org":"Hansen, Peter Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0001-9972-1649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Roberto","key":"galeazzipau","last":"Galeazzi","locid":"b66b869e-5eed-4d7a-bc66-7f5bc41d96f7","name":"Galeazzi, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0002-6047-7922","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"palmapau","last":"Palma","name":"Palma, Marco","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Libonati","key":"brockpau","last":"Brock","name":"Brock, Andreas Libonati","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patrizio","key":"marianipau","last":"Mariani","locid":"c0cde97e-57b6-4ec0-9870-bdf77f2bc1b3","name":"Mariani, Patrizio","orcid":"0000-0002-8015-1583","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/fusion59988.2024.10706512","eisbn":["9781737749769"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2024 27th International Conference on Information Fusion (FUSION)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207692230"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ab955fc5-e971-4f02-a325-003cad6eaf8b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Autonomous Inspection and Data Fusion for Maritime Critical Infrastructures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764354","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Obesity rates have nearly tripled in the past 50 years, and by 2030 more than 1 billion individuals worldwide are projected to be obese. This creates a significant economic strain due to the associated non-communicable diseases. The root cause is an energy expenditure imbalance, owing to an interplay of lifestyle, environmental, and genetic factors. Obesity has a polygenic genetic architecture; however, single genetic variants with large effect size are etiological in a minority of cases. These variants allowed the discovery of novel genes and biology relevant to weight regulation and ultimately led to the development of novel specific treatments. Methods: We used a case-control approach to determine metabolic differences between individuals homozygous for a loss-of-function genetic variant in the small integral membrane protein 1 (SMIM1) and the general population, leveraging data from five cohorts. Metabolic characterization of SMIM1−/− individuals was performed using plasma biochemistry, calorimetric chamber, and DXA scan. Findings: We found that individuals homozygous for a loss-of-function genetic variant in SMIM1 gene, underlying the blood group Vel, display excess body weight, dyslipidemia, altered leptin to adiponectin ratio, increased liver enzymes, and lower thyroid hormone levels. This was accompanied by a reduction in resting energy expenditure. Conclusion: This research identified a novel genetic predisposition to being overweight or obese. It highlights the need to investigate the genetic causes of obesity to select the most appropriate treatment given the large cost disparity between them. Funding: This work was funded by the National Institute of Health Research, British Heart Foundation, and NHS Blood and Transplant.","author_count":496,"contributors":["Stefanucci, Luca","Moslemi, Camous","Tomé, Ana R.","Virtue, Samuel","Bidault, Guillaume","Gleadall, Nicholas S.","Watson, Laura P.E.","Kwa, Jing E.","Burden, Frances","Farrow, Samantha","Banasik, Karina","Bay, Jakob","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Brodersen, Thorsten","Brunak, Søren","Burgdorf, Kristoffer","Chalmer, Mona Ameri","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Dowsett, Joseph","Erikstrup, Christian","Feenstra, Bjarke","Geller, Frank","Gudbjartsson, Daniel","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Hindhede, Lotte","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Jemec, Gregor","Jensen, Bitten Aagaard","Kaspersen, Kathrine Agergård","Kjerulff, Bertram","Kogelman, Lisette","Hørup Larsen, Margit Anita","Louloudis, Ioannis","Lundgaard, Agnete","Susan, no-firstname","Mikkelsen, Christina","Nissen, Ioanna","Nyegaard, Mette","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Pedersen, Ole B.","Henriksen, Alexander Pil","Rohde, Palle Duun","Rostgaard, Klaus","Schwinn, Michael","Stefansson, Kari","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sørensen, Erik","þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas","Westergaard, David","Chen, Ji","Spracklen, Cassandra N.","Marenne, Gaëlle","Varshney, Arushi","Corbin, Laura J.","Luan, Jian'an","Willems, Sara M.","Wu, Ying","Zhang, Xiaoshuai","Horikoshi, Momoko","Boutin, Thibaud S.","Mägi, Reedik","Waage, Johannes","Li-Gao, Ruifang","Katie Chan, Kei Hang","Yao, Jie","Anasanti, Mila D.","Chu, Audrey Y.","Claringbould, Annique","Heikkinen, Jani","Hong, Jaeyoung","Hottenga, Jouke Jan","Huo, Shaofeng","Kaakinen, Marika A.","Louie, Tin","März, Winfried","Moreno-Macias, Hortensia","Ndungu, Anne","Nelson, Sarah C.","Nolte, Ilja M.","North, Kari E.","Raulerson, Chelsea K.","Ray, Debashree","Rohde, Rebecca","Rybin, Denis","Schurmann, Claudia","Sim, Xueling","Southam, Loz","Stewart, Isobel D.","Wang, Carol A.","Wang, Yujie","Wu, Peitao","Zhang, Weihua","Ahluwalia, Tarunveer S.","Appel, Emil V.R.","Bielak, Lawrence F.","Brody, Jennifer A.","Burtt, Noël P.","Cabrera, Claudia P.","Cade, Brian E.","Chai, Jin Fang","Chai, Xiaoran","Chang, Li Ching","Chen, Chien Hsiun","Chen, Brian H.","Chitrala, Kumaraswamy Naidu","Chiu, Yen Feng","de Haa