nal":"Science of the Total Environment","pages":"156944","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"844"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126857404"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7f758092-d51b-4c2c-9ad7-e5609899fdd0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mercury contamination and potential health risks to Arctic seabirds and shorebirds","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-202260","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this paper is to investigate how service-based organizations can continuously capitalize on knowledge across their multiple project management office (PMO) setup to fast-track adaptation and deliver value to their clients. Based on literature on PMO and knowledge management, this paper utilizes a Design Science Research (DSR) methodology and contributes to theory and practice in three ways. First, it links knowledge management activities with the multiple PMO-setup. Second, it conceptualizes the PMO as a temporary organization within organizational contexts. Lastly, this paper contributes methodologically as it illustrates the utility of DSR to address the interplay between knowledge management and cross- and inter-organizational PMOs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Birn, Jonas","Mortensen, Nicholas","Hansen, Lars Kristian","Svejvig, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-204270"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-17","place":"Winterthur, ch","start":"2022-06-15","title":"EURAM 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"capitalizing on knowledge in a multiple pmo setup a design science research approach","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-204270","ids":["au-8346ebb5-cf7e-4245-80ed-34ae71ab32b0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3418D8969BB8C37EE9C9C7CC64089FC6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"birnpau","last":"Birn","name":"Birn, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Nicholas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Kristian","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"87bfbaf0-825b-4e79-894d-3a2771a7242c","name":"Hansen, Lars Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-3714-4123","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"svejvigpau","last":"Svejvig","locid":"40558617-c35b-464e-a0f6-7a2940494271","name":"Svejvig, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-8758-4031","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8346ebb5-cf7e-4245-80ed-34ae71ab32b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Capitalizing on Knowledge in a Multiple PMO-setup: : A Design Science Research Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-204270","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Highly reliable situation awareness is a main driver to enhance safety via autonomous technology in the marine industry. Groundings, ship collisions and collisions with bridges illustrate the need for enhanced safety. Authority for a computer to suggest actions or to take command, would be able to avoid some accidents where human misjudgement was a core reason. Autonomous situation awareness need be conducted with extreme confidence to let a computer algorithm take command. The anticipation of how a situation can develop is by far the most difficult step in situation awareness, and anticipation is the subject of this article. The IMO International Regulations for Preventing Collisions at Sea (COLREGS), describe the regulatory behaviours of marine vessels relative to each other, and correct interpretation of situations is instrumental to safe navigation. Based on a breakdown of COLREGS rules, this article presents a framework to represent manoeuvring behaviours that are expected when all vessels obey the rules. The article shows how nested finite automata can segregate situation assessment from decision making and provide a testable and repeatable algorithm. The suggested method makes it possible to anticipate own ship and other vessels’ manoeuvring in a multi-vessel scenario. The framework is validated using scenarios from a full-mission simulator.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","Hansen, Nicholas","Dittmann, Kjeld","Blanke, Mogens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-315909"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Papageorgiou, Dimitrios"],"keyword":["Autonomous vessels","COLREGs representation","Finite state automata","Situation awareness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anticipation of ship behaviours in multi vessel scenarios","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oceaneng.2022.112777","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-315909","identifier":[{"id":"85136192031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-26392487-7926-4072-b4af-e4db819da6ae"],"keyword":["Autonomous vessels","Behaviour anticipation","COLREGS representation","Dual-view assesment","Finite-state automata","Multi-vessel encounter","Situation awareness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2566855AEA4F481B5D4EB5715ED731B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/293785758/1_s2.0_S0029801822020601_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oceaneng.2022.112777","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dimitrios","key":"papageorgioupau","last":"Papageorgiou","locid":"1731579d-4271-42df-864e-6013a9ce795c","name":"Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","orcid":"0000-0002-4900-4083","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicholas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d79b2754-2197-48d4-bc85-9c4578cf9fb3","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0001-9972-1649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"dittmannpau","last":"Dittmann","locid":"71cc977f-3480-48c6-9a56-7d77b7d7bc54","name":"Dittmann, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0001-6263-6096","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"blankepau","last":"Blanke","locid":"a4238b5e-294f-4ee2-a56d-a9f9473eb715","name":"Blanke, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-9181-9518","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.oceaneng.2022.112777","issn":["00298018","18735258"],"issn_org":["00298018"],"issue":"Part 2","journal":"Ocean Engineering","paperid":"112777","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ocean Engineering","volume":"266"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136192031"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-26392487-7926-4072-b4af-e4db819da6ae"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Anticipation of ship behaviours in multi-vessel scenarios","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-315909","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: DNA hypomethylation at the F2RL3 (F2R like thrombin or trypsin receptor 3) locus has been associated with both smoking and atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease; whether these smoking-related associations form a pathway to disease is unknown. F2RL3 encodes protease-activated receptor 4, a potent thrombin receptor expressed on platelets. Given the role of thrombin in platelet activation and the role of thrombus formation in myocardial infarction, alterations to this biological pathway could be important for ischemic cardiovascular disease. Methods: We conducted multiple independent experiments to assess whether DNA hypomethylation at F2RL3 in response to smoking is associated with risk of myocardial infarction via changes to platelet reactivity. Using cohort data (N=3205), we explored the relationship between smoking, DNA hypomethylation at F2RL3, and myocardial infarction. We compared platelet reactivity in individuals with low versus high DNA methylation at F2RL3 (N=41). We used an in vitro model to explore the biological response of F2RL3 to cigarette smoke extract. Finally, a series of reporter constructs were used to investigate how differential methylation could impact F2RL3 gene expression. Results: Observationally, DNA methylation at F2RL3 mediated an estimated 34% of the smoking effect on increased risk of myocardial infarction. An association between methylation group (low/high) and platelet reactivity was observed in response to PAR4 (protease-activated receptor 4) stimulation. In cells, cigarette smoke extract exposure was associated with a 4.9% to 9.3% reduction in DNA methylation at F2RL3 and a corresponding 1.7-(95% CI, 1.2-2.4, P=0.04) fold increase in F2RL3 mRNA. Results from reporter assays suggest the exon 2 region of F2RL3 may help control gene expression. Conclusions: Smoking-induced epigenetic DNA hypomethylation at F2RL3 appears to increase PAR4 expression with potential downstream consequences for platelet reactivity. Combined evidence here not only identifies F2RL3 DNA methylation as a possible contributory pathway from smoking to cardiovascular disease risk but from any feature potentially influencing F2RL3 regulation in a similar manner.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Corbin, Laura J.","White, Stephen J.","Taylor, Amy E.","Williams, Christopher M.","Taylor, Kurt","Van Den Bosch, Marion T.","Teasdale, Jack E.","Jones, Matthew","Bond, Mark","Harper, Matthew T.","Falk, Louise","Groom, Alix","Hazell, Georgina G.J.","Paternoster, Lavinia","Munafò, Marcus R.","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Bojesen, Stig E","Relton, Caroline","Min, Josine L.","Davey Smith, George","Mumford, Andrew D.","Poole, Alastair W.","Timpson, Nicholas J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488375"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Manchester Metropolitan University","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University of Bristol","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Blood Platelets","DNA methylation","Epigenomics","Myocardial Infarction","Smoking","Thrombin","Tobacco"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epigenetic regulation of i f000000000002rl000000000003 i associates with myocardial infarction and platelet function","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCRESAHA.121.318836","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488375","identifier":[{"id":"35012325","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85124056710","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8812435","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku