{"abstract":"Autonomous surface vessels comprise complex automated systems with advanced onboard sensors. These help establish situation awareness and perform many of the complex tasks required for safe navigation. However, situations occur that require assistance by a human proxy. If not physically present on board, information digestion and sharing between human and machine become crucial to maintain safe operation. This paper addresses the co-design of on-board systems and a Remote Control Centre (RCC). Using the international regulations on watch-keeping (STCW) as a basis, the paper discuss how an autonomous system is designed to meet the STCW requirements. It is discussed how the autonomous system is made aware of the state of the vessel, its surroundings, on-board defects or navigational challenges and shared with the RCC in a collaborating system perspective.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dittmann, Kjeld","Hansen, Nicholas","Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","Jensen, Signe","Lützen, Marie","Blanke, Mogens"],"cuid":["S02-092.55-035039"],"event":{"acronym":"CAMS","end":"2021-09-24","place":"Online event","start":"2021-09-22","title":"13<sup>th</sup> IFAC Conference on Control Applications in Marine Systems, Robotics, and Vehicles","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Dittmann, Kjeld"],"keyword":["Autonomous Ship","Autonomous marine crafts","Regulations","Remote operation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomous surface vessel with remote human on the loop system design for stcw compliance","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ifacol.2021.10.097","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.55-035039","identifier":[{"id":"85120889573","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6a957998-8445-4510-be8b-1c1dce01dfc9","sdu-99bedf70-b6f7-4a15-b823-bd3a1d494682"],"keyword":["Autonomous Ship","Autonomous marine crafts","Regulations","Remote Operation","Safe Navigation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FB8E7F6CA4FC69F999B25A81D5B53A68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/196378640/1_s2.0_S2405896321014993_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/262110363/0025_CAMS_Preprint_23_09_2021.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ifacol.2021.10.097","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Law","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Law, EU & International Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"dittmannpau","last":"Dittmann","locid":"71cc977f-3480-48c6-9a56-7d77b7d7bc54","name":"Dittmann, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0001-6263-6096","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicholas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d79b2754-2197-48d4-bc85-9c4578cf9fb3","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0001-9972-1649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dimitrios","key":"papageorgioupau","last":"Papageorgiou","locid":"1731579d-4271-42df-864e-6013a9ce795c","name":"Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","orcid":"0000-0002-4900-4083","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4b868722-cf87-48e4-ad56-2ee03afb439a","name":"Jensen, Signe","orcid":"0000-0002-2814-7659","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"lützenpau","last":"Lützen","locid":"04a22e6f-e980-4634-b8ef-4d18d634e0a2","name":"Lützen, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-6036-5234","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"blankepau","last":"Blanke","locid":"a4238b5e-294f-4ee2-a56d-a9f9473eb715","name":"Blanke, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-9181-9518","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ifacol.2021.10.097","issn":["24058963"],"issn_org":["24058971"],"issue":"16","journal":"IFAC-PapersOnLine","pages":"224-231","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"IFAC-PapersOnLine","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120889573"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6a957998-8445-4510-be8b-1c1dce01dfc9","sdu-99bedf70-b6f7-4a15-b823-bd3a1d494682"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Autonomous Surface Vessel with Remote Human on the Loop: System Design for STCW Compliance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.55-035039","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Autonomous systems strive to obtain salient features that include computer intelligence for obtaining situation awareness, decision support to a human navigator, or for facilitating autonomous decision-making in unmanned vehicles. This paper considers the case of autonomous marine surface vehicles, where high-quality decision support will be instrumental for obtaining a periodically unattended bridge and for approval of unmanned bridge operation with fallback through remote operation. The proposed design focuses on a sovereign-based architecture that facilitates safety, resilience and cyber-security. We address central elements of risk in the development and approval of autonomous systems; we analyze the challenges associated with testing, commissioning and maintenance of a highly complex cyber-physical system, and describe design principles for the sovereign agents architecture.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dittmann, Kjeld","Hansen, Nicholas","Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","Blanke, Mogens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313695"],"event":{"end":"2021-10-01","place":"Saint-Raphaël, fr","start":"2021-09-29","title":"5<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Control and Fault-Tolerant Systems","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomy for ships a sovereign agents architecture for reliability and safety by design","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258017390/0062_SysTol_Preprint_29_09_2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-313695","identifier":[{"id":"85119479692","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1e923588-8e45-47cc-9da6-8bf398688e30"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2F38076F447B39759D0BB978D58A192"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258017390/0062_SysTol_Preprint_29_09_2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"dittmannpau","last":"Dittmann","locid":"71cc977f-3480-48c6-9a56-7d77b7d7bc54","name":"Dittmann, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0001-6263-6096","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d79b2754-2197-48d4-bc85-9c4578cf9fb3","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0001-9972-1649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dimitrios","key":"papageorgioupau","last":"Papageorgiou","locid":"1731579d-4271-42df-864e-6013a9ce795c","name":"Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","orcid":"0000-0002-4900-4083","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"blankepau","last":"Blanke","locid":"a4238b5e-294f-4ee2-a56d-a9f9473eb715","name":"Blanke, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-9181-9518","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/systol52990.2021.9595889","isbn":["9781665431583"],"pages":"50-57","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 5<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Control and Fault-Tolerant Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119479692"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1e923588-8e45-47cc-9da6-8bf398688e30"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Autonomy for Ships: A Sovereign Agents Architecture for Reliability and Safety by Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313695","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Autonomy at different levels is envisaged to provide decision support, to enable navigation with temporally unattended bridge or have the navigator placed remotely, being able to take command if required. For this purpose, methods for computer-based situation awareness are needed to avoid risks of collision. Correct interpretation of a situation is crucial, and all navigation decisions must be based on the COLREGs. This paper presents a discrete-eventsystems-based framework that facilitates autonomous interpretation of the situation in which the own ship is. This can be used for COLREGs-compliant decision planning when all vessels navigate according to the rules. The proposed framework comprises a set of coupled finite-state deterministic automata and segregates situation understanding from anticipation. The suggested formalism is analysed with respect to avoidance of deadlocks and shows how synchronisation of vessel-specific automata modules is achieved. Simulations illustrate the concept using realistic scenarios.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Nicholas","Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","Blanke, Mogens","Galeazzi, Roberto","Lûtzen, M.","Mogensen, J.","Bennedsen, M.","Hansen, D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335848"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anticipation","Autonomous vessels","COLREGs representation","Discrete event systems","Finite state automata","Situation assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Svendborg International Maritime Academy"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"colregs based situation awareness for marine vessels a discrete event systems approach","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/220003741/2020_ifac_pnh_dp_mb_rg_ml_mh_jm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335848","identifier":[{"id":"85105053997","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-68bd1dd8-6da3-48b4-91d4-bd6b7f3a6405"],"keyword":["Anticipation","Autonomous situation awareness","Autonomous vessels","COLREGs representation","Discrete-event systems","Finite-state automata","Situation assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57A85D33253C57A3283ECCED6ACE693D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/220003741/2020_ifac_pnh_dp_mb_rg_ml_mh_jm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Svendborg International Maritime Academy"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Nicholas","key":"hansennicholaspau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d79b2754-2197-48d4-bc85-9c4578cf9fb3","name":"Hansen, Nicholas","name_org":"Hansen, Peter Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0001-9972-1649","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dimitrios","key":"papageorgioudimitriospau","last":"Papageorgiou","locid":"1731579d-4271-42df-864e-6013a9ce795c","name":"Papageorgiou, Dimitrios","orcid":"0000-0002-4900-4083","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"blankemogenspau","last":"Blanke","locid":"a4238b5e-294f-4ee2-a56d-a9f9473eb715","name":"Blanke, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-9181-9518","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"galeazzirobertopau","last":"Galeazzi","locid":"b66b869e-5eed-4d7a-bc66-7f5bc41d96f7","name":"Galeazzi, Roberto","orcid":"0000-0002-6047-7922","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"lûtzenmpau","last":"Lûtzen","name":"Lûtzen, M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"mogensenjpau","last":"Mogensen","name":"Mogensen, J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"bennedsenmpau","last":"Bennedsen","name":"Bennedsen, M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"hansendpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, D.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ifacol.2020.12.1453","issn":["24058963"],"issue":"2","journal":"IFAC-PapersOnLine","pages":"14501-14508","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"IFAC-PapersOnLine","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105053997"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-68bd1dd8-6da3-48b4-91d4-bd6b7f3a6405"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"COLREGs-based Situation Awareness for Marine Vessels - a Discrete Event Systems Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335848","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Mendelian randomization (MR) studies use genetic variation associated with modifiable exposures to assess their possible causal relationship with outcomes and aim to reduce potential bias from confounding and reverse causation. Objective: To develop the STROBE-MR Statement as a stand-alone extension to the STROBE (Strengthening the Reporting of Observational Studies in Epidemiology) guideline for the reporting of MR studies. Design, Setting, and Participants: The development of the STROBE-MR Statement followed the Enhancing the Quality and Transparency of Health Research (EQUATOR) framework guidance and used the STROBE Statement as a starting point to draft a checklist tailored to MR studies. The project was initiated in 2018 by reviewing the literature on the reporting of instrumental variable and MR studies. A group of 17 experts, including MR methodologists, MR study design users, developers of previous reporting guidelines, and journal editors, participated in a workshop in May 2019 to define the scope of the Statement and draft the checklist. The draft checklist was published as a preprint in July 2019 and discussed on the preprint platform, in social media, and at the 4th Mendelian Randomization Conference. The checklist was then revised based on comments, further refined through 2020, and finalized in July 2021. Findings: The STROBE-MR checklist is organized into 6 sections (Title and Abstract, Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion, and Other Information) and includes 20 main items and 30 subitems. It covers both 1-sample and 2-sample MR studies that assess 1 or multiple exposures and outcomes, and addresses MR studies that follow a genome-wide association study and are reported in the same article. The checklist asks authors to justify why MR is a helpful method to address the study question and state prespecified causal hypotheses. The measurement, quality, and selection of genetic variants must be described and attempts to assess validity of MR-specific assumptions should be well reported. An item on data sharing includes reporting when the data and statistical code required to replicate the analyses can be accessed. Conclusions and Relevance: STROBE-MR provides guidelines for reporting MR studies. Improved reporting of these studies could facilitate their evaluation by editors, peer reviewers, researchers, clinicians, and other readers, and enhance the interpretation of their results.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Skrivankova, Veronika W.","Richmond, Rebecca C.","Woolf, Benjamin A.R.","Yarmolinsky, James","Davies, Neil M.","Swanson, Sonja A.","Vanderweele, Tyler J.","Higgins, Julian P.T.","Timpson, Nicholas J.","Dimou, Niki","Langenberg, Claudia","Golub, Robert M.","Loder, Elizabeth W.","Gallo, Valentina","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Davey Smith, George","Egger, Matthias","Richards, J. Brent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408438"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","France","Germany","Netherlands","Norway","South Africa","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","American Medical Association","Berlin Institute of Health","British Medical Journal","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Harvard University","International Agency for Research on Cancer","King's College London","McGill University","Northwestern University","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Queen Mary University of London","University of Bern","University of Bristol","University of Cambridge","University of Cape Town","University of Groningen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strengthening the reporting of observational studies i