{"abstract":"Bipolar disorder is a heritable mental illness with complex etiology. We performed a genome-wide association study of 41,917 bipolar disorder cases and 371,549 controls of European ancestry, which identified 64 associated genomic loci. Bipolar disorder risk alleles were enriched in genes in synaptic signaling pathways and brain-expressed genes, particularly those with high specificity of expression in neurons of the prefrontal cortex and hippocampus. Significant signal enrichment was found in genes encoding targets of antipsychotics, calcium channel blockers, antiepileptics and anesthetics. Integrating expression quantitative trait locus data implicated 15 genes robustly linked to bipolar disorder via gene expression, encoding druggable targets such as HTR6, MCHR1, DCLK3 and FURIN. Analyses of bipolar disorder subtypes indicated high but imperfect genetic correlation between bipolar disorder type I and II and identified additional associated loci. Together, these results advance our understanding of the biological etiology of bipolar disorder, identify novel therapeutic leads and prioritize genes for functional follow-up studies.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Mullins, Niamh","Forstner, Andreas J","O'Connell, Kevin S","Coombes, Brandon","Coleman, Jonathan R I","Qiao, Zhen","Als, Thomas Damm","Bigdeli, Tim B","Børte, Sigrid","Bryois, Julien","Charney, Alexander W","Drange, Ole Kristian","Gandal, Michael J","Hagenaars, Saskia P","Ikeda, Masashi","Kamitaki, Nolan","Kim, Minsoo","Krebs, Kristi","Panagiotaropoulou, Georgia","Schilder, Brian M","Sloofman, Laura G","Steinberg, Stacy","Trubetskoy, Vassily","Winsvold, Bendik S","Won, Hong-Hee","Abramova, Liliya","Adorjan, Kristina","Agerbo, Esben","Al Eissa, Mariam","Albani, Diego","Alliey-Rodriguez, Ney","Anjorin, Adebayo","Antilla, Verneri","Antoniou, Anastasia","Awasthi, Swapnil","Baek, Ji Hyun","Bækvad-Hansen, Marie","Bass, Nicholas","Bauer, Michael","Beins, Eva C","Bergen, Sarah E","Birner, Armin","Pedersen, Carsten Bøcker","Pedersen, Marianne Giørtz","Grove, Jakob","Mattheisen, Manuel","Xu, Wei","Børglum, Anders D","Mors, Ole","Mortensen, Preben Bo"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014329"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["HUNT All-In Psychiatry"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Canada","Estonia","Germany","Greece","Iceland","Japan","Norway","Russia","South Korea","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Broad Institute","Fujita Health University","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Karolinska Institutet","King's College London","Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, Massachusetts, USA.","Mayo Clinic Jacksonville, FL","Medical University of Graz","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Russian Academy of Medical Sciences","SUNY Downstate Medical Center","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","Sungkyunkwan University","Technische Universität Dresden","University College London","University Health Network","University of Athens","University of Bonn","University of California at San Diego","University of Chicago","University of Oslo","University of Queensland","University of Tartu","University of Würzburg","Würzburg University Hospital","deCODE Genetics"],"keyword":["Bipolar Disorder genetics","Case Control Studies","Chromosomes Human genetics","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Human","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Major Histocompatibility Complex genetics","Multifactorial Inheritance genetics","Phenotype","Quantitative Trait Loci genetics","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"OT":["