:"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"N.","key":"raghurampedh","last":"Raghuram","name":"Raghuram, N.","rank":25,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"S.","key":"reispedh","last":"Reis","name":"Reis, S.","rank":26,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"M.","key":"bekundapedh","last":"Bekunda","name":"Bekunda, M.","rank":27,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-58065-0_25","eisbn":["9783030580650"],"isbn":["9783030580643"],"pages":"363-376","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Perspectives on how to get there for regions with too much and too little nitrogen","title":"Just Enough Nitrogen"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149056003"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5b643c19-26eb-4b28-9fbb-e3e4aa01a264","ku-aaea03b5-dae9-4a1c-8c09-c987190ad538"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DNMARK: Danish Nitrogen Mitigation Assessment: : Research and Know-how for a Sustainable, Low-Nitrogen Food Production","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.77-019315","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Simple Summary Novel biomarkers that can identify melanoma patients responding to immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy are urgently needed. As high T-cell infiltration and low fibrotic activity are associated with response, we aimed to examine the serum biomarker potential of granzyme B degraded type IV collagen (C4G) products in combination with the fibrosis biomarker PRO-C3. We found that high C4G combined with low PRO-C3 has the potential to identify patients responding to immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy suggesting that these biomarkers may provide a non-invasive tool for patient selection and therapeutic decision-making in the future. A T-cell permissive tumor microenvironment, characterized by the presence of activated T cells and low fibrotic activity is crucial for response to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). Granzyme B has been shown to promote T-cell migration through the basement membrane by the degradation of type IV collagen. In this study, we evaluated the biomarker potential of measuring granzyme B-mediated degradation of type IV collagen (C4G) in combination with a fibroblast activation biomarker (PRO-C3) non-invasively for identifying metastatic melanoma patients responding to the ICI ipilimumab. A monoclonal antibody was generated against C4G and used to develop a competitive electro-chemiluminescence immunoassay. C4G and PRO-C3 were measured in pretreatment serum from metastatic melanoma patients (n = 54). The C4G assay was found specific for a granzyme B-generated neo-epitope on type IV collagen. The objective response rate (ORR) was 2.6-fold higher (18% vs. 7%) in patients with high C4G levels (>25th percentile) vs. low levels (","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jensen, Christina","Sinkeviciute, Dovile","Madsen, Daniel Hargbøl","Önnerfjord, Patrik","Hansen, Morten","Schmidt, Henrik","Karsdal, Morten Asser","Svane, Inge Marie","Willumsen, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S02-094.87-019585"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Christina"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Cancer progression","Collagen","Extracellular matrix","Fibrosis","Immune checkpoint inhibitor","Immunotherapy","Ipilimumab","MATRIX","Melanoma","Predictive biomarker","Survival","T cell infiltration","Tumor microenvironment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"granzyme b degraded type iv collagen products in serum identify melanoma patients responding to immune checkpoint blockade","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers12102786","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.87-019585","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7601429","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000584069900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"32998446","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85091714288","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5f431f5c-3b1c-4811-a896-b4e1cdff2d72","ku-7739a9e9-6e43-40ec-80f8-df95f42e8d43"],"keyword":["Biomarker","CANCER PROGRESSION","Collagen","Extracellular matrix","Fibrosis","Immune checkpoint inhibitor","Immunotherapy","Ipilimumab","MATRIX","Melanoma","PREDICTIVE BIOMARKER","SURVIVAL","T-cell infiltration","Tumor microenvironment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-249BA9BBD7D0F24A50EE0A647B75379E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers12102786","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251410302/cancers_12_02786_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Erler Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oncology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"05a281b4-bcef-4f1e-ab39-1b6c4800a896","name":"Jensen, Christina","orcid":"0000-0002-3485-7307","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"sinkeviciutepau","last":"Sinkeviciute","name":"Sinkeviciute, Dovile","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel Hargbol","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Daniel Hargbol","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrik","key":"önnerfjordpau","last":"Önnerfjord","name":"Önnerfjord, Patrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Patrik","key":"onnerfjordpau","last":"Onnerfjord","name":"Onnerfjord, Patrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"834188a5-a600-41a5-a8a1-9e34c3837141","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Asser","key":"karsdalpau","last":"Karsdal","name":"Karsdal, Morten Asser","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge Marie","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"12c124a9-b64d-4b36-9bbd-c1665658101d","name":"Svane, Inge Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-9451-6037","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"willumsenpau","last":"Willumsen","name":"Willumsen, Nicholas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32998446"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers12102786","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"10","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"2786","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091714288"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Nordic Bioscience","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5f431f5c-3b1c-4811-a896-b4e1cdff2d72","ku-7739a9e9-6e43-40ec-80f8-df95f42e8d43"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Granzyme B Degraded Type IV Collagen Products in Serum Identify Melanoma Patients Responding to Immune Checkpoint Blockade","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.87-019585","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To determine if the Food Standards Agency nutrient profiling system (FSAm-NPS), which grades the nutritional quality of food products and is used to derive the Nutri-Score front-of-packet label to guide consumers towards healthier food choices, is associated with mortality. DESIGN: Population based cohort study. SETTING: European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC) cohort from 23 centres in 10 European countries. PARTICIPANTS: 521 324 adults; at recruitment, country specific and validated dietary questionnaires were used to assess their usual dietary intakes. A FSAm-NPS score was calculated for each food item per 100 g content of energy, sugars, saturated fatty acids, sodium, fibre, and protein, and of fruit, vegetables, legumes, and nuts. The FSAm-NPS dietary index was calculated for each participant as an energy weighted mean of the FSAm-NPS score of all foods consumed. The higher the score the lower the overall nutritional quality of the diet. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE: Associations between the FSAm-NPS dietary index score and mortality, assessed using multivariable adjusted Cox proportional hazards regression models. RESULTS: After exclusions, 501 594 adults (median follow-up 17.2 years, 8 162 730 person years) were included in the analyses. Those with a higher FSAm-NPS dietary index score (highest versus lowest fifth) showed an increased risk of all cause mortality (n=53 112 events from non-external causes; hazard ratio 1.07, 95% confidence interval 1.03 to 1.10, P<0.001 for trend) and mortality from cancer (1.08, 1.03 to 1.13, P<0.001 for trend) and diseases of the circulatory (1.04, 0.98 to 1.11, P=0.06 for trend), respiratory (1.39, 1.22 to 1.59, P<0.001), and digestive (1.22, 1.02 to 1.45, P=0.03 for trend) systems. The age standardised absolute rates for all cause mortality per 10 000 persons over 10 years were 760 (men=1237; women=563) for those in the highest fifth of the FSAm-NPS dietary index score and 661 (men=1008; women=518) for those in the lowest fifth. CONCLUSIONS: In this large multinational European cohort, consuming foods with a higher FSAm-NPS score (lower nutritional quality) was associated with a higher mortality for all causes and for cancer and diseases of the circulatory, respiratory, and digestive systems, supporting the relevance of FSAm-NPS to characterise healthier food choices in the context of public health policies (eg, the Nutri-Score) for European populations. This is important considering ongoing discussions about the potential implementation of a unique nutrition labelling system at the European Union level.","author_count":57,"contributors":["Deschasaux, Mélanie","Huybrechts, Inge","Julia, Chantal","Hercberg, Serge","Egnell, Manon","Srour, Bernard","Kesse-Guyot, Emmanuelle","Latino-Martel, Paule","Biessy, Carine","Casagrande, Corinne","Murphy, Neil","Jenab, Mazda","Ward, Heather A","Weiderpass, Elisabete","Overvad, Kim","Tjønneland, Anne","Rostgaard-Hansen, Agnetha Linn","Boutron-Ruault, Marie-Christine","Mancini, Francesca Romana","Mahamat-Saleh, Yahya","Kühn, Tilman","Katzke, Verena","Bergmann, Manuela M","Schulze, Matthias B","Trichopoulou, Antonia","Karakatsani, Anna","Peppa, Eleni","Masala, Giovanna","Agnoli, Claudia","De Magistris, Maria Santucci","Tumino, Rosario","Sacerdote, Carlotta","Boer, Jolanda Ma","Verschuren, Wm Monique","van der Schouw, Yvonne T","Skeie, Guri","Braaten, Tonje","Redondo, M Luisa","Agudo, Antonio","Petrova, Dafina","Colorado-Yohar, Sandra M","Barricarte, Aurelio","Amiano, Pilar","Sonestedt, Emily","Ericson, Ulrika","Otten, Julia","Sundström, Björn","Wareham, Nicholas J","Forouhi, Nita G","Vineis, Paolo","Tsilidis, Konstantinos K","Knuppel, Anika","Papier, Keren","Ferrari, Pietro","Riboli, Elio","Gunter, Marc J","Touvier, Mathilde"],"cuid":["S02-099.96-019264"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, South","E