 Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between nutritional profiles of foods underlying Nutri-Score front-of-pack labels and mortality : EPIC cohort study in 10 European countries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.96-019264","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"C57BL/6J-related mouse strains are widely used animal models for diet-induced obesity (DIO). Multiple vendors breed C57BL/6J-related substrains which may introduce genetic drift and environmental confounders such as microbiome differences. To address potential vendor/substrain specific effects, we compared DIO of C57BL/6J-related substrains from three different vendors: C57BL/6J (Charles Rivers), C57BL/6JBomTac (Taconic Bioscience) and C57BL/6JRj (Janvier). After local acclimatization, DIO was induced by either a high-fat diet (HFD, 60% energy from fat) or western diet (WD, 42% energy from fat supplemented with fructose in the drinking water). All three groups on HFD gained a similar amount of total body weight, yet the relative amount of fat percentage and mass of inguinal- and epididymal white adipose tissue (iWAT and eWAT) was lower in C57BL/6JBomTac compared to the two other C57BL/6J-releated substrains. In contrast to HFD, the three groups on WD responded differently in terms of body weight gain, where C57BL/6J was particularly prone to WD. This was associated with a relative higher amount of eWAT, iWAT, and liver triglycerides. Although the HFD and WD had significant impact on the microbiota, we did not observe any major differences between the three groups of mice. Together, these data demonstrate significant differences in HFD- and WD-induced adiposity in C57BL/6J-related substrains, which should be considered in the design of animal DIO studies.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Siersbæk, Majken Storm","Ditzel, Nicholas","Hejbøl, Eva Kildall","Præstholm, Stine Marie","Markussen, Lasse Kruse","Avolio, Fabio","Li, Lingzi","Lehtonen, Lasse","Hansen, Axel Kornerup","Schrøder, Henrik Daa","Krych, Lukasz","Mandrup, Susanne","Langhorn, Louise","Bollen, Peter","Grøntved, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-042906"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Grøntved, Lars"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry Photon","Animals","Body Weight","Diet High Fat","Glucose administration dosage","Insulin blood","Liver metabolism","Mice","Mice Inbred C57BL","Obesity genetics","Organ Size","Species Specificity","Triglycerides metabolism","Weight Gain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"c000000000057bl 000000000006j substrain differences in response to high fat diet intervention","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-70765-w","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Janvier Labs, SCANBUR, and Taconic are acknowledged for providing the animals needed for this study at our disposal. Animal technicians Camilla Rasmussen, Liv Holm, and Martine Nielsen, and laboratory technician Vivi Monrad from Biomedical laboratory, University of Southern Denmark, are acknowledged for their enthusiastic and skillful contribution to the study. This work was supported by the Biomedical Laboratory, University of Southern Denmark and the Danish National Research Foundation through a grant (#141) to the Center for Functional Genomics and Tissue Plasticity (ATLAS)."],"id":"S02-100.00-042906","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7441320","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85089587391","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32820201","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-61a8b22e-d464-4a2f-8b8b-4cfbdb4f6ace","sdu-fbcebe01-2dcd-4020-9d85-74d7f4095696"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry, Photon","Animals","Body Weight","Diet, High-Fat","Glucose/administration & dosage","Insulin/blood","Liver/metabolism","Mice","Mice, Inbred C57BL","Obesity/genetics","Organ Size","Species Specificity","Triglycerides/metabolism","Weight Gain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F47B9D4CD0D3FA226D0F4E63E7F4C77D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/247982491/C57BL6J_substrain_differences_in_response_to_high_fat_diet_intervention.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-70765-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/172429885/s41598_020_70765_w.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Morphogenesis and Differentiation Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, ATLAS - Center for Functional Genomics and Tissue Plasticity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of South