{"abstract":"The neuronal primary cilium and centriolar satellites have functions in neurogenesis, but little is known about their roles in the postnatal brain. We show that ablation of pericentriolar material 1 in the mouse leads to progressive ciliary, anatomical, psychomotor, and cognitive abnormalities. RNAseq reveals changes in amine- and G-protein coupled receptor pathways. The physiological relevance of this phenotype is supported by decreased available dopamine D2 receptor (D2R) levels and the failure of antipsychotic drugs to rescue adult behavioral defects. Immunoprecipitations show an association with Pcm1 and D2Rs. Finally, we sequence PCM1 in two human cohorts with severe schizophrenia. Systematic modeling of all discovered rare alleles by zebrafish in vivo complementation reveals an enrichment for pathogenic alleles. Our data emphasize a role for the pericentriolar material in the postnatal brain, with progressive degenerative ciliary and behavioral phenotypes; and they support a contributory role for PCM1 in some individuals diagnosed with schizophrenia. The role of ciliary/centriolar components in the postnatal brain is unclear. Here, the authors show via ablation of Pcm1 in mice that degenerative ciliary/centriolar phenotypes induce neuroanatomical and behavioral changes. Sequencing of PCM1 in human cohorts and zebrafish in vivo complementation suggests PCM1 mutations can contribute to schizophrenia.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Monroe, Tanner O.","Garrett, Melanie E.","Kousi, Maria","Rodriguiz, Ramona M.","Moon, Sungjin","Bai, Yushi","Brodar, Steven C.","Soldano, Karen L.","Savage, Jeremiah","Fritz-Hansen, Thomas","Muzny, Donna M.","Gibbs, Richard A.","Barak, Lawrence","Sullivan, Patrick F.","Ashley-Koch, Allison E.","Sawa, Akira","Wetsel, William C.","Werge, Thomas","Katsanis, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416990"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ann & Robert H Lurie Childrens Hosp Chicago, Ann & Robert H. Lurie Children's Hospital of Chicago, Adv Ctr Translat & Genet Med ACT GeM, Stanley Manne Childrens Res Inst","Baylor College of Medicine","Broad Institute","Duke University","Johns Hopkins University","Karolinska Institutet","The University of Chicago"],"keyword":["Centrosome","Disease","Framework","Genetic association","Hydrocephalus","Metaanalysis","Mutations","RARE","Recruitment","Replication"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Kangwon Natl Univ, Kangwon National University, Dept Biol Sci"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pcm000000000001 is necessary for focal ciliary integrity and is a candidate for severe schizophrenia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-19637-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416990","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7677393","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000595682600008","type":"wos"},{"id":"33214552","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85096345816","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-275b7530-f25e-4d78-a15f-eb8be557d886"],"keyword":["CENTROSOME","DISEASE","FRAMEWORK","GENETIC ASSOCIATION","HYDROCEPHALUS","METAANALYSIS","MUTATIONS","RARE","RECRUITMENT","REPLICATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4891F749960385F967B8FEBB29319A27"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-19637-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258283765/s41467_020_19637_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","m