Claudia","key":"langenbergpau","last":"Langenberg","name":"Langenberg, Claudia","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nita G.","key":"forouhipau","last":"Forouhi","name":"Forouhi, Nita G.","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas J.","key":"warehampau","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Nicholas J.","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33064751"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pmed.1003394","issn":["15491277","15491676"],"issn_org":["15491277"],"issue":"10","journal":"PLoS Medicine","paperid":"e1003394","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLoS Medicine","title_org":"PLOS Medicine","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85093706249"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a404113a-130f-430b-9b81-6cee21279cfb","au-8357f02e-887c-4ca4-bb47-b982ae8e13ea"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The association between circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D metabolites and type 2 diabetes in European populations : A meta-analysis and Mendelian randomisation analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.74-007924","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: This study aimed to improve early risk stratification in the emergency department by creating a simple blood test score based on routine biomarkers and assess its predictive ability for 30-day mortality of acutely admitted patients. METHODS: This was a secondary analysis of data from the TRIAGE II study. It included unselected acutely admitted medical and surgical patients, who had albumin, C-reactive protein, creatinine, haemoglobin, leukocytes, potassium, sodium and thrombocytes levels analysed upon admission. Patients were classified according to the number of biomarker results outside the reference range into four risk groups termed \"very low\", \"low\", \"intermediate\", and \"high\" with 0-1, 2-3, 4-5 and 6-8 abnormal biomarker results, respectively. Logistic regression was used to calculate odds ratios for 30-day mortality and receiver operating characteristic was used to test the discriminative value. The primary analysis was done in patients triaged with ADAPT (Adaptive Process Triage). Subsequently, we analysed two other cohorts of acutely admitted patients. RESULTS: The TRIAGE II cohort included 17,058 eligible patients, 30-day mortality was 5.2%. The primary analysis included 7782 patients. Logistic regression adjusted for age and sex showed an OR of 24.1 (95% CI 14.9-41.0) between the very low- and the high-risk group. The area under the curve (AUC) was 0.79 (95% CI 0.76-0.81) for the blood test score in predicting 30-day mortality. The subsequent analyses confirmed the results. CONCLUSIONS: A blood test score based on number of routine biomarkers with an abnormal result was a predictor of 30-day mortality in acutely admitted patients.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Roenhoej Rønhøj, Rasmus","Hasselbalch, Rasmus B","Schultz, Martin","Pries-Heje, Mia","Plesner, Louis L","Ravn, Lisbet","Lind, Morten","Jensen, Birgitte N","Hoei-Hansen Høi-Hansen, Thomas","Carlson, Nicholas","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Rasmussen, Lars S","Rasmussen, Line J H","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Koeber Køber, Lars","Iversen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007650"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Biomarkers metabolism","Clinical Chemistry Tests","Emergency Service Hospital","Emergency department","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Mortality","Patient Admission","Risk stratification","Triage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"abnormal routine blood tests as predictors of mortality in acutely admitted patients","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85077715296&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007650","identifier":[{"id":"31843666","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85077715296","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9dc80284-2d2e-432f-8506-ce45399808f0","ku-a4392565-b60b-4025-9548-951d7ba1125b"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Biomarkers/metabolism","Clinical Chemistry Tests","Emergency Service, Hospital","Emergency department","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Mortality","Patient Admission","Risk stratification","Routine biomarkers","Triage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-35D832E52C1DAB7ACDE92725C22BA260"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Den