b":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The chapter concentrates on the development of a system designed to constrain the pitch interval in western music. Western tuning systems, according to Knakkergaard, developed out of the Ancient Greek's mystical fascination with the number 4. Thus, the Ancient Greek's beliefs and imaginations are very much alive today in a musical system that both regulates and guides compositional imagination, and this remains the case even with the apparent freedom offered music by digitalization.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","Walther-Hansen, Mads","Knakkergaard, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086878"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["SYSTEM","Tuning","diatonism"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction volume 000000000002","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dbp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-086878","ids":["aau-7ea37925-93d9-47aa-836f-588d3dab6046"],"keyword":["diatonism","system","tuning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-15958BAE277E7E07CA82C9895046EABE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music & Sound Knowledge Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture,