earch?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026418","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Mark Grimshaw-Aagaard takes issue with the objectification and quantification of (and often outright attempts to eliminate) imprecision and subjectivity in the natural sciences, particularly in acoustics and the field of audio testing. Instead, he argues, experiences of vagueness and ambiguity are essential to an imagining of sound, where that imagination aids in the experiencing of an external world. Such imagination, Grimshaw-Aagaard contends, performs a vital role in the emergence of perceptual hypotheses about the external world and thus the presence of our selves in the context of the nonself that is the external world.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-067978"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ambiguity","Imagination","Sound","Vagueness"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the necessity of vagueness and ambiguity to the imagining of sound","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.oxfordhandbooks.com/view/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190460167.001.0001/oxfordhb-9780190460167-e-5","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-067978","ids":["aau-3dd905a6-e20e-4b30-abcb-3f71f7e8f6e7"],"keyword":["Ambiguity","Imagination","Sound","Vagueness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-DE917282B14EE6482CD21453008A99D5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music & Sound Knowledge Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark Nicholas","key":"grimshawaagaardpau","last":"Grimshaw-Aagaard","locid":"673322d2-f25b-4f45-93b2-ba1c4c9fdbc5","name":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0003-0485-6087","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark","key":"grimshawaagaardpedh","last":"Grimshaw-Aagaard","name":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mads","key":"waltherhansenpedh","last":"Walther-Hansen","name":"Walther-Hansen, Mads","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"knakkergaardpedh","last":"Knakkergaard","name":"Knakkergaard, Martin","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190460167.013.5","isbn":["9780190460167"],"pages":"105-113","place":"New York","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Oxford Handbook of Sound and Imagination","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3dd905a6-e20e-4b30-abcb-3f71f7e8f6e7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Necessity of Vagueness and Ambiguity to the Imagining of Sound","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-067978","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The Introduction to Volume 2 of The Oxford Handbook of Sound and Imagination serves three purposes. First, it broadly sets out the aims and arc of the handbook and in particular its multidisciplinary scope. Second, it describes the handbook’s genesis and the principles that guided its development. Third, the Introduction lays out the content of each of the five parts of the second volume (“Musical Performance, \" “Systems and Technologies, \" “Psychology, \" “Aesthetics, \" and “Posthumanism”) and briefly summarizes each chapter.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","Walther-Hansen, Mads","Knakkergaard, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072744"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Auditory imagery","Imagination","Music","Musicology","Psychoacoustics","Sound","Sound Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction volume 000000000002","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dbp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85111865030&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-072744","identifier":[{"id":"85111865030","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4e57dc46-6823-4832-aed0-9f7e89e6268b"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Auditory imagery","Imagination","Music","Musicology","Psychoacoustics","Sound","Sound studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-15958BAE277E7E07CA82C9895046EABE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music & Sound Knowledge Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"grimshawaagaardpau","last":"Grimshaw-Aagaard","locid":"673322d2-f25b-4f45-93b2-ba1c4c9fdbc5","name":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","name_org":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark","orcid":"0000-0003-0485-6087","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"waltherhansenpau","last":"Walther-Hansen","locid":"73804945-3d74-4f54-a2db-ab1be9009c09","name":"Walther-Hansen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0001-5746-5093","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"knakkergaardpau","last":"Knakkergaard","locid":"e887ba8e-8061-4957-a4d3-ba8aff24d7d6","name":"Knakkergaard, Martin","orcid":"0000-0003-1091-8504","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190460242.013.77","eisbn":["9780190460242"],"pages":"1-11","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Oxford Handbook of Sound and Imagination, Volume 2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111865030"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4e57dc46-6823-4832-aed0-9f7e89e6268b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Introduction : Volume 2","type":"Book Preface, Encycl. Entry","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-072744","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Global sensitivity analysis (GSA) and derivative-free optimisation (DFO) methods share a common task which is the multiple evaluation of black box models. For sensitivity analysis the value sets in the sample hypercube are evaluated and the output vector is stored to then post-process this input-output data relation with different GSA methods. In case of DFO, initial estimates of the variables are sent to the black box model and then the result is evaluated in respect to a stopping criterion. If the criterion isn't met then a new input set is defined and sent to the black box model, whereas the evaluation loop stops if the criterion is satisfied and an optimum is found. We developed a Python based COM-interface to the ProII process simulator to analyse several case studies. Sensitivity analysis methods were applied to a heat pump system [1] and a molecular distillation process [2] to retrieve sensitivity indices for the consumption of power (COP) or the beta-carotene recovery subject to critical temperature, critical pressure and acentric factor which the Soave-Redlich-Kwong equation of state depends on. Sobol sensitivity analysis and Morris screening were performed for both cases. A three-step glycerol purification process was optimised via DFO to obtain the optimal values for the operating parameters (TUnit, PUnit) and the feed flowrate to the system of three evaporation units. The optimizer RBFopt and surrogate modelling, namely polynomial chaos expansion, were applied to solve for the operating point close to the optimum. The results show that the Python-COM interface is a valuable tool to connect process models in a simulator with more advanced sensitivity and optimisation techniques.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jones, Mark Nicholas","Hansen, C. H.","Forero-Hernandez, Hector","Sarup, B.","Sin, Gürkan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346055"],"event":{"end":"2019-03-20","place":"Magdeburg, de","start":"2019-03-18","title":"1st International Young Professionals Conference on Process Engineering (YCPE 2019)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALFA","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ALFA","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monte carlo based sensitivity analysis and derivative free optimisation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/171229114/Monte_Carlo_based_Sensitivity_Analysis_and_Derivative_free_Optimisation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-346055","identifier":[{"id":"85065135627","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8b1a6567-d56e-4a69-bd0e-aed58daa92df"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-75E8171B37CBF869E018D34876B31635"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/171229114/Monte_Carlo_based_Sensitivity_Analysis_and_Derivative_free_Optimisation.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, KT Consortium","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, PROSYS - Process and Systems Engineering Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"alfa laval nordic","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ALFA","l3nl":"Alfa Laval","l3nn":"Alfa Laval Nordic","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alfa Laval Nordic","namevar":["Alfa Laval"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ALFA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. N.","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","locid":"393576ee-5f26-4882-8946-39eb7c8e1ba0","name":"Jones, Mark Nicholas","name_org":"Jones, M. N.","orcid":"0000-0002-7588-0482","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C. H.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, C. H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H.","key":"forerohernandezpau","last":"Forero-Hernandez","locid":"47b1ae66-069f-4219-8fc9-7e611be6828d","name":"Forero-Hernandez, Hector","name_org":"Forero-Hernandez, H.","orcid":"0000-0002-3477-6873","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"saruppau","last":"Sarup","name":"Sarup, B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"G.","key":"sinpau","last":"Sin","locid":"4c35984e-28c5-43c9-9a4b-c7ac589bf597","name":"Sin, Gürkan","name_org":"Sin, G.","orcid":"0000-0003-0513-4502","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Alfa Laval","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8b1a6567-d56e-4a69-bd0e-aed58daa92df"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Monte Carlo based Sensitivity Analysis and Derivative-free Optimisation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-346055","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia, defined as an increase in plasma triglyceride-containing lipoproteins following a fat meal, is a potential risk predictor of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease and other chronic diseases. Several non-modifiable factors (genetics, age, sex and menopausal status) and lifestyle factors (diet, physical activity, smoking status, obesity, alcohol and medication use) may influence postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia. This narrative review considers the studies published over the last decade that evaluated postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia. Additionally, the genetic determinants of postprandial plasma triglyceride levels, the types of meals for studying postprandial triglyceride response, and underlying conditions (e.g. familial dyslipidaemias, diabetes mellitus, metabolic syndrome, non-alcoholic fatty liver and chronic kidney disease) that are associated with postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia are reviewed; therapeutic aspects are also considered.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Kolovou, Genovefa D","Watts, Gerald F","Mikhailidis, Dimitri P","Pérez-Martínez, Pablo","Mora, Samia","Bilianou, Helen","Panotopoulos, George","Katsiki, Niki","Ooi, Teik C","Lopez-Miranda, José","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Tentolouris, Nicholas","Nordestgaard, Børge G"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-430445"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia revisited in the era of non fasting lipid profile testing a 000000002019 expert panel statement narrative review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-430445","identifier":[{"id":"85071782649","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31309820","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3df5b8d3-3168-43d4-9a13-1a70f0abee19"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-8-D894145D410361FFDC54DB162FCF3393"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Genovefa D","key":"kolovoupau","last":"Kolovou","name":"Kolovou, Genovefa D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerald F","key":"wattspau","last":"Watts","name":"Watts, Gerald F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dimitri P","key":"mikhailidispau","last":"Mikhailidis","name":"Mikhailidis, Dimitri P","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pablo","key":"pérezmartínezpau","last":"Pérez-Martínez","name":"Pérez-Martínez, Pablo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Samia","key":"morapau","last":"Mora","name":"Mora, Samia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helen","key":"bilianoupau","last":"Bilianou","name":"Bilianou, Helen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"George","key":"panotopoulospau","last":"Panotopoulos","name":"Panotopoulos, George","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niki","key":"katsikipau","last":"Katsiki","name":"Katsiki, Niki","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Teik C","key":"ooipau","last":"Ooi","name":"Ooi, Teik C","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"lopezmirandapau","last":"Lopez-Miranda","name":"Lopez-Miranda, José","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"tybjærghansenpau","last":"Tybjærg-Hansen","locid":"452a492e-c869-41e5-b60e-1d2a542287cf","name":"Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicholas","key":"tentolourispau","last":"Tentolouris","name":"Tentolouris, Nicholas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Børge G","key":"nordestgaardpau","last":"Nordestgaard","locid":"733103b5-ddc2-416f-a686-48e694154a82","name":"Nordestgaard, Børge G","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31309820"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/1570161117666190503123911","issn":["15701611","18756212"],"issn_org":["15701611"],"issue":"5","journal":"Current Vascular Pharmacology","pages":"515-537","status":"p","title":"Current Vascular Pharmacology","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068043866","2-s2.0-85071782649"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3df5b8d3-3168-43d4-9a13-1a70f0abee19"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Postprandial Hypertriglyceridaemia Revisited in the Era of Non-Fasting Lipid Profile Testing : A 2019 Expert Panel Statement, Narrative Review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-430445","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: We characterised the phenotypic consequence of genetic variation at the PCSK9 locus and compared findings with recent trials of pharmacological inhibitors of PCSK9. Methods: Published and individual participant level data (300,000+ participants) were combined to construct a weighted PCSK9 gene-centric score (GS). Seventeen randomized placebo controlled PCSK9 inhibitor trials were included, providing data on 79,578 participants. Results were scaled to a one mmol/L lower LDL-C concentration. Results: The PCSK9 GS (comprising 4 SNPs) associations with plasma lipid and apolipoprotein levels were consistent in direction with treatment effects. The GS odds ratio (OR) for myocardial infarction (MI) was 0.53 (95% CI 0.42; 0.68), compared to a PCSK9 inhibitor effect of 0.90 (95% CI 0.86; 0.93). For ischemic stroke ORs were 0.84 (95% CI 0.57; 1.22) for the GS, compared to 0.85 (95% CI 0.78; 0.93) in the drug trials. ORs with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) were 1.29 (95% CI 1.11; 1.50) for the GS, as compared to 1.00 (95% CI 0.96; 1.04) for incident T2DM in PCSK9 inhibitor trials. No genetic associations were observed for cancer, heart failure, atrial fibrillation, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, or Alzheimer's disease - outcomes for which large-scale trial data were unavailable. Conclusions: Genetic variation at the PCSK9 locus recapitulates the effects of therapeutic inhibition of PCSK9 on major blood lipid fractions and MI. While indicating an increased risk of T2DM, no other possible safety concerns were shown; although precision was moderate.","author_count":165,"contributors":["Schmidt, Amand F.","Holmes, Michael V.","Preiss, David","Swerdlow, Daniel I.","Denaxas, Spiros","Fatemifar, Ghazaleh","Faraway, Rupert","Finan, Chris","Valentine, Dennis","Fairhurst-Hunter, Zammy","Hartwig, Fernando Pires","Horta, Bernardo Lessa","Hypponen, Elina","Power, Christine","Moldovan, Max","Van Iperen, Erik","Hovingh, Kees","Demuth, Ilja","Norman, Kristina