:{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Novo Nordisk","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Private Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","danish diabetes academy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c6fc7b48-40e2-4832-95ec-4d17d7944955","au-a7ce83f0-1e23-41f2-8efc-9b7ac4e931e7","ku-5c5713af-03e4-4c1c-b20a-42c62ae04d17","sdu-70bd17b6-6637-462f-ae92-8f858eb989b5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations of Mitochondrial and Nuclear Mitochondrial Variants and Genes with Seven Metabolic Traits","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.82-009557","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Mark Grimshaw-Aagaard takes issue with the objectification and quantification of (and often outright attempts to eliminate) imprecision and subjectivity in the natural sciences, particularly in acoustics and the field of audio testing. Instead, he argues, experiences of vagueness and ambiguity are essential to an imagining of sound, where that imagination aids in the experiencing of an external world. Such imagination, Grimshaw-Aagaard contends, performs a vital role in the emergence of perceptual hypotheses about the external world and thus the presence of our selves in the context of the nonself that is the external world.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","Walther-Hansen, Mads","Knakkergaard, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072386"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ambiguity","Imagination","Sound","Vagueness"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction volume 000000000001","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dbp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.oxfordhandbooks.com/view/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190460167.001.0001/oxfordhb-9780190460167-e-40","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-072386","ids":["aau-4d087e64-1b51-491b-b039-7b9298ef26a6"],"keyword":["Ambiguity","Imagination","Sound","Vagueness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-35D423CF577EC43A29A6ED5A9119D30E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanit