AU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Oxford Handbook of Sound and Imagination Vol. 2","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081832","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Mark Grimshaw-Aagaard addresses the role of sound in the creation of presence in virtual and actual worlds. He argues that imagination is a central part of the generation and selection of perceptual hypotheses—models of the world in which we can act—that emerge from what Grimshaw-Aagaard calls the “exo-environment” (the sensory input) and the “endo-environment” (the cognitive input). Grimshaw-Aagaard further divides the exo-environment into a primarily auditory and a primarily visual dimension and he deals with the actual world of his own apartment and the virtual world of first-person-shooter computer games in order to exemplify how we perceptually construct an environment that allows for the creation of presence.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"presence environment and sound and the role of imagination","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.oxfordhandbooks.com/view/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190460167.001.0001/oxfordhb-9780190460167-e-33","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-088030","ids":["aau-828cd158-b624-4a13-8085-7d314be102cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3D5D8D5FBDDA68552E7FC1019FBBBB22"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music & Sound Knowledge Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"grimshawaagaardpau","last":"Grimshaw-Aagaard","locid":"673322d2-f25b-4f45-93b2-ba1c4c9fdbc5","name":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","name_org":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark","orcid":"0000-0003-0485-6087","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark","key":"grimshawpedh","last":"Grimshaw","name":"Grimshaw, Mark","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mads","key":"waltherhansenpedh","last":"Walther-Hansen","name":"Walther-Hansen, Mads","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"knakkergaardpedh","last":"Knakkergaard","name":"Knakkergaard, Martin","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190460167.013.33","isbn":["9780190460167"],"pages":"669-681","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Oxford Handbook of Sound and Imagination","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-828cd158-b624-4a13-8085-7d314be102cd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Presence, Environment, and Sound and the Role of Imagination","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088030","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"β-Mannans are plant cell wall polysaccharides that are commonly found in human diets. However, a mechanistic understanding into the key populations that degrade this glycan is absent, especially for the dominant Firmicutes phylum. Here, we show that the prominent butyrate-producing Firmicute Roseburia intestinalis expresses two loci conferring metabolism of β-mannans. We combine multi-“omic” analyses and detailed biochemical studies to comprehensively characterize loci-encoded proteins that are involved in β-mannan capturing, importation, de-branching and degradation into monosaccharides. In mixed cultures, R. intestinalis shares the available β-mannan with Bacteroides ovatus, demonstrating that the apparatus allows coexistence in a competitive environment. In murine experiments, β-mannan selectively promotes beneficial gut bacteria, exemplified by increased R. intestinalis, and reduction of mucus-degraders. Our findings highlight that R. intestinalis is a primary degrader of this dietary fiber and that this metabolic capacity could be exploited to selectively promote key members of the healthy microbiota using β-mannan-based therapeutic interventions.","author_count":13,"contributors":["La Rosa, Sabina Leanti","Leth, Maria Louise","Michalak, Leszek","Hansen, Morten Ejby","Pudlo, Nicholas A.","Glowacki, Robert","Pereira, Gabriel","Workman, Christopher","Arntzen, Magnus","Pope, Phillip B.","Martens, Eric C.","Abou Hachem, Maher","Westereng, Bjørge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-321899"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Westereng, Bjørge"],"country":["Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Life Sciences","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the human gut firmicute roseburia intestinalis is a primary degrader of dietary β mannans","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-019-08812-y","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors wish to thank M. Kjos (NMBU) for assistance with immunofluorescence microscopy. This work was supported by a grant from the Research Council of Norway (244259). Additional funding was from a Graduate School DTU Scholarship, Lyngby, Denmark for M.L.L. and from the Independent Research Fund Denmark, Natural Sciences (DFF, FNU) by a Research Project 2 grant (Grant ID: 4002–00297B) to M.A.H. Carlsberg Foundation is also acknowledged for an instrument grant for purchase of the ITC200 calorimeter to M.A.H."],"id":"S01-000.00-321899","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6385246","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85062024856","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30796211","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-3a473faa-d5d1-4f52-a88a-ff377e0bf28f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0095B3D3D590C1E314AE8A4683EF51B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-019-08812-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/169853519/s41467_019_08812_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of life sciences","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Life Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, Protein Glycoscience and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabina Leanti","key":"larosapau","last":"La Rosa","name":"La Rosa, Sabina Leanti","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Louise","key":"lethpau","last":"Leth","locid":"5c4c23c9-6b7f-43d5-9172-3df4c1acc0f2","name":"Leth, Maria Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-5668-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leszek","key":"michalakpau","last":"Michalak","name":"Michalak, Leszek","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Ejby","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"1cae1449-131e-4b5e-9f76-eee6c06f3169","name":"Hansen, Morten Ejby","orcid":"0000-0003-2099-3591","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas A.","key":"pudlopau","last":"Pudlo","name":"Pudlo, Nicholas A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"glowackipau","last":"Glowacki","name":"Glowacki, Robert","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gabriel","key":"pereirapau","last":"Pereira","name":"Pereira, Gabriel","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christopher T.","key":"workmanpau","last":"Workman","locid":