{"abstract":"Residual vascular risk exists despite the aggressive lowering of Low-Density Lipoprotein Cholesterol (LDL-C). A contributor to this residual risk may be elevated fasting, or non-fasting, levels of Triglyceride (TG)-rich lipoproteins. Therefore, there is a need to establish whethe a standardised Oral Fat Tolerance Test (OFTT) can improve atherosclerotic Cardiovascular (CV) Disease (ASCVD) risk prediction in addition to a fasting or non-fasting lipid profile. An expert panel considered the role of postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia (as represented by an OFTT) in predicting ASCVD. The panel updated its 2011 statement by considering new studies and various patient categories. The recommendations are based on expert opinion since no strict endpoint trials have been performed. Individuals with fasting TG concentration <1 mmol/L (89 mg/dL) commonly do not have an abnormal response to an OFTT. In contrast, those with fasting TG concentration ≥2 mmol/L (175 mg/dL) or nonfasting ≥2.3 mmol/L (200 mg/dL) will usually have an abnormal response. We recommend considering postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia testing when fasting TG concentrations and non-fasting TG concentrations are 1-2 mmol/L (89-175 mg/dL) and 1.3-2.3 mmol/L (115-200 mg/dL), respectively as an additional investigation for metabolic risk prediction along with other risk factors (obesity, current tobacco abuse, metabolic syndrome, hypertension, and diabetes mellitus). The panel proposes that an abnormal TG response to an OFTT (consisting of 75 g fat, 25 g carbohydrate and 10 g proteins) is >2.5 mmol/L (220 mg/dL). Postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia is an emerging factor that may contribute to residual CV risk. This possibility requires further research. A standardised OFTT will allow comparisons between investigational studies. We acknowledge that the OFTT will be mainly used for research to further clarify the role of TG in relation to CV risk. For routine practice, there is a considerable support for the use of a single non-fasting sample.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Kolovou, Genovefa D","Watts, Gerald F","Mikhailidis, Dimitri P","Pérez-Martínez, Pablo","Mora, Samia","Bilianou, Helen","Panotopoulos, George","Katsiki, Niki","Ooi, Teik C","Lopez-Miranda, José","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Tentolouris, Nicholas","Nordestgaard, Børge G"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-502903"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"postprandial hypertriglyceridaemia revisited in the era of non fasting lipid profile testing a 000000002019 expert panel statement main text","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-502903","identifier":[{"id":"31060488","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068043866","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b747eac4-9262-4a1f-86ed-b2cf125ca56e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-8-D894145D410361FFDC54DB162FCF3393"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Genovefa D","key":"kolovoupau","last":"Kolovou","name":"Kolovou, Genovefa D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerald F","key":"wattspau","last":"Watts","name":"Watts, Gerald F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dimitri P","key":"mikhailidispau","last":"Mikhailidis","name":"Mikhailidis, Dimitri P","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pablo","key":"pérezmartínezpau","last":"Pérez-Martínez","name":"Pérez-Martínez, Pablo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Samia","key":"morapau","last":"Mora","name":"Mora, Samia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helen","key":"bilianoupau","last":"Bilianou","name":"Bilianou, Helen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"George","key":"panotopoulospau","last":"Panotopoulos","name":"Panotopoulos, George","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niki","key":"katsikipau","last":"Katsiki","name":"Katsiki, Niki","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Teik C","key":"ooipau","last":"Ooi","name":"Ooi, Teik C","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"lopezmirandapau","last":"Lopez-Miranda","name":"Lopez-Miranda, José","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"tybjærghansenpau","last":"Tybjærg-Hansen","locid":"452a492e-c869-41e5-b60e-1d2a542287cf","name":"Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicholas","key":"tentolourispau","last":"Tentolouris","name":"Tentolouris, Nicholas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Børge G","key":"nordestgaardpau","last":"Nordestgaard","locid":"733103b5-ddc2-416f-a686-48e694154a82","name":"Nordestgaard, Børge G","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31060488"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/1570161117666190507110519","issn":["15701611","18756212"],"issn_org":["15701611"],"issue":"5","journal":"Current Vascular Pharmacology","pages":"498-514","status":"p","title":"Current Vascular Pharmacology","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068043866","2-s2.0-85071782649"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b747eac4-9262-4a1f-86ed-b2cf125ca56e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Postprandial Hypertriglyceridaemia Revisited in the Era of Non-Fasting Lipid Profile Testing : A 2019 Expert Panel Statement, Main Text","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-502903","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Triage systems with limited room for clinical judgment are used by emergency departments (EDs) worldwide. The Copenhagen Triage Algorithm (CTA) is a simplified triage system with a clinical assessment. METHODS: The trial was a non-inferiority, two-center cluster-randomized crossover study where CTA was compared to a local adaptation of Adaptive Process Triage (ADAPT). CTA involves initial categorization based on vital signs with a final modification based on clinical assessment by an ED nurse. We used 30-day mortality with a non-inferiority margin at 0.5%. Predictive performance was compared using Receiver Operator Characteristics. RESULTS: We included 45,347 patient visits, 23,158 (51%) and 22,189 (49%) were triaged with CTA and ADAPT respectively with a 30-day mortality of 3.42% and 3.43% (P = 0.996) a difference of 0.01% (95% CI: -0.34 to 0.33), which met the non-inferiority criteria. Mortality at 48 hours was 0.62% vs. 0.71%, (P = 0.26) and 6.38% vs. 6.61%, (P = 0.32) at 90 days for CTA and ADAPT. CTA triaged at significantly lower urgency level (P<0.001) and was superior in predicting 30-day mortality, Area under the curve: 0.67 (95% CI 0.65-0.69) compared to 0.64 for ADAPT (95% CI 0.62-0.66) (P = 0.03). There were no significant differences in rate of admission to the intensive care unit, length of stay, waiting time nor rate of readmission within 30 or 90 days. CONCLUSION: A novel triage system based on vital signs and a clinical assessment by an ED nurse was non-inferior to a traditional triage algorithm by short term mortality, and superior in predicting 30-day mortality. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinicaltrials.gov NCT02698319.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Pries-Heje, Mia","Schultz, Martin","Plesner, Louis Lind","Ravn, Lisbet","Lind, Morten","Greibe, Rasmus","Jensen, Birgitte Nybo","Høi-Hansen, Thomas","Carlson, Nicholas","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Rasmussen, Lars S","Iversen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-088.50-008188"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"OT":["Department of Anaesthesia, Center of Head and Orthopaedics, Rigshospitalet, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the copenhagen triage algorithm is non inferior to a traditional triage algorithm a cluster randomized study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0211769","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.50-008188","identifier":[{"id":"000457744200048","type":"wos"},{"id":"30716123","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85061059751","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6361446","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-a9acbe0d-4c88-402e-8867-c8f20faaa5f2","ku-dee55564-f1eb-4e98-99b8-10a80f42304d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9BBBD593C22A35731BD14ADBA7271518"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/295952170/Hasselbalch_et_al._2019_PLOS_ONE_0211769.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/224598807/journal.pone.0211769.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0211769","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospital