{"abstract":"The aim of this work is to compare angle of incidence (AOI) measurement setups for solar cells between laboratories with such capability. For the first time, we compare relative light transmission measurements among eight laboratories, whose measurement techniques include indoor and outdoor methods. We present the relative transmission measurements on three 156 mm x 156 mm crystalline-Si (c-Si) samples with different surface textures. The measurements are compared using the expanded uncertainties provided by each laboratory. Five of the eight labs showed an agreement better than ±2% to the weighted mean between AOIs from -75° to 70°. At AOIs of ±80° and ±85°, the same five labs showed a worst case deviation to the weighted mean of -3% to 5% and 0% to 18%, respectively. When measurement uncertainty is considered, the results show that measurements at the highest incidence angle of ±85° are problematic, as measurements from four out of the six labs reporting uncertainty were found non-comparable within their stated uncertainties. At 85° AOI a high to low range of up to 75% was observed between all eight laboratories.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Riedel, Nicholas","Santamaria Lancia, Adrian Alejo","Amdemeskel, Mekbib Wubishet","Thorsteinsson, Sune","Poulsen, Peter Behrensdorff","Plag, Fabian","Kröger, Ingo","Slooff, Lenneke H.","Jansen, Mark J.","Carr, Anna J.","Manshanden, Petra","Bliss, Martin","Betts, Tom","Jauregui, Iñigo Petrina","Mayo, Mikel Ezquer","Balenzategui, Jose L.","Roldan, Ruben","Kräling, Ulli","Baarah, Ghassan","Iandolo, Beniamino","Davidsen, Rasmus Schmidt","Thorseth, Anders","Dam-Hansen, Carsten","Benatto, Gisele Alves dos Reis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346054"],"event":{"end":"2018-09-28","place":"Brussels, be","start":"2018-09-24","title":"35th European Photovoltaic Solar Energy Conference and Exhibition","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CIEMAT","Energy Research Centre of the Netherlands","Fraunhofer Institute for Solar Energy Systems","Loughborough University","National Renewable Energy Center","Physikalisch-Technische Bundesanstalt","University of Applied Sciences and Arts of Southern Switzerland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interlaboratory comparison of methodologies for measuring the angle of incidence dependence of solar cells","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4229/35thEUPVSEC20182018-5BO.10.4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-346054","ids":["dtu-8b1a3190-9537-4eb5-86a5-1a358a6c2650"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-108EE1AAFE962C699B72F1803AB2B1A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/160489340/thorsteh.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4229/35thEUPVSEC20182018-5BO.10.4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Photovoltaic Materials and Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"physikalisch technische bundesanstalt","