ode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"George","key":"kirovgeorgepau","last":"Kirov","name":"Kirov, George","rank":66,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael J","key":"owenmichaeljpau","last":"Owen","name":"Owen, Michael J","rank":67,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael C","key":"odonovanmichaelcpau","last":"O'Donovan","name":"O'Donovan, Michael C","rank":68,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"James T. R.","key":"waltersjamestrpau","last":"Walters","name":"Walters, James T. R.","rank":69,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29483656"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41588-018-0059-2","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"3","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"381-389","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042546549"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-47b7cc59-a2b1-4426-9640-d8ea58ffdfe2","ku-29b0fa32-4499-4d9d-b000-4ec11d1d6cb9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Common schizophrenia alleles are enriched in mutation-intolerant genes and in regions under strong background selection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-017882","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Use of proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) has been associated with cardiovascular disease amongst patients not on antiplatelet therapy. The associations of PPI use, duration and dose, with risk of first-time ischemic stroke and myocardial infarction (MI) are poorly understood. Methods: All Danish individuals with no prior history of MI or stroke, who had an elective upper gastrointestinal endoscopy performed between 1997 and 2012, were identified from nationwide registries. We used multiple Poisson regression to test associations with current PPI use and its dose and used multiple cause-specific Cox regression and g-formula methods to analyze long-term use. Results: Amongst 214 998 individuals, during a median follow-up of 5.8 years, there were 7916 ischemic strokes and 5608 MIs. Current PPI exposure was associated with significantly higher rates of both ischemic stroke (Hazard ratio (HR) 1.13; 95% confidence interval (CI) 1.08–1.19) and MI (HR 1.31, CI 1.23–1.39) after adjusting for age, sex, comorbidities and concomitant medication. High-dose PPI was associated with increased rates of ischemic stroke (HR 1.31, CI 1.21–1.42) and MI (HR 1.43, CI 1.30–1.57). Histamine H2 receptor antagonists (H2RAs) use was not significantly associated with ischemic stroke (HR 1.02, CI 0.84–1.24) or MI (HR 1.15, CI 0.92–1.43). Long-term users of PPIs, compared with nonusers, had a 29% (CI 5%-59%) greater absolute risk of ischemic stroke and a 36% (CI 7%-73%) greater risk of MI within a 6-month period. Conclusion: Use of PPIs was associated with increased risks of first-time ischemic stroke and MI, particularly amongst long-term users and at high doses.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Sehested, Thomas S G","Gerds, Thomas A","Fosbøl, Emil L","Hansen, Peter W","Charlot, Mette G","Carlson, Nicholas","Hlatky, Mark A","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Gislason, Gunnar H"],"cuid":["S03-085.82-002891"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sehested, T. S.G."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Myocardial Infarction","Observational Study","Proton pump inhibitors","Registries","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"OT":["Department of Cardiovascular Epidemiology and Research, The Danish Heart Foundation, Vognmagergade 7, 3rd floor, 1120, Copenhagen K, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term use of proton pump inhibitors dose response relationship and associated risk of ischemic stroke and myocardial infarction","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85042268206&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["1From the Department of Cardiovascular Epidemiology and Research, The Danish Heart Foundation, Copenhagen K;2Department of Biostatistics, Copenhagen University, Copenhagen; 3The Heart Centre, Copenhagen University Hospital, Rigshospitalet, Denmark; 4Department of Health Research and Policy, Department of Medicine, Stanford University School of Medicine, Stanford, CA, USA; 5Department of Cardiology, Copenhagen University Hospital, Herlev and Gentofte; 6Department of Internal Medicine, Gastroenterology section, Holbaek Hospital, Holbaek; 7Department of Health, Science and Technology, Department of Cardiology and Epidemiology/ Biostatistics, Aalborg University, Aalborg University Hospital, Hellerup; and 8The National Institute of Public Health, University of Southern Denmark, Copenhagen, Denmark The Danish Heart Foundation supported this study. The Danish Heart Foundation had no influence on the study design, interpretation of results or the decision to submit the manuscript for publication. E.L.F. was previously supported by a project-specific research grant from Janssen Pharmaceuticals and has received research funding from the Lundbeck Foundation and Bristol-Myers Squibb outside the scope of the present work. GHG has received research funding from Boehringer Ingelheim, Pfizer, BMS, AstraZeneca and Bayer and declares ownership of stocks in Lundbeck A/ S, Novo Nordisk A/S and ALK Abello pharmaceuticals outside the scope of the present work. CTP has received grant and personal fees from Pfizer, Merck & Co, Sanofi and Cardiome outside the scope of the present work. There is no other disclosure. All authors state independence from the funders."],"id":"S03-085.82-002891","identifier":[{"id":"29024109","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85042268206","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000425521000004","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-3a764a71-ce9a-4dbc-a4cf-58d3f3406311","ku-32a77ca8-efbe-4808-8af3-eba8b952a6f4","sdu-b9b6b97f-1df3-4e91-9979-ee7840e3cc33"],"keyword":["myocardial infarction","observational study","proton pump inhibitors","registries","stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-C3A2A3A0CAC362B04609BE74170312CC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Cardiovascular Epidemiology and Research, The Danish Heart Foundation, Vognmagergade 7, 3rd floor, 1120, Copenhagen K, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish heart foundati