{"abstract":"Biosynthesis of steviol glycosides in planta proceeds via two cytochrome P450 enzymes (CYPs): kaurene oxidase (KO) and kaurenoic acid hydroxylase (KAH). KO and KAH function in succession with the support of a NADPH-dependent cytochrome P450 reductase (CPR) to convert kaurene to steviol. This work describes a platform for recombinant production of steviol glucosides (SGs) in Saccharomyces cerevisiae, demonstrating the full reconstituted pathway from the simple sugar glucose to the SG precursor steviol. With a focus on optimization of the KO-KAH activities, combinations of functional homologues were tested in batch growth. Among the CYPs, novel KO75 (CYP701) and novel KAH82 (CYP72) outperformed their respective functional homologues from Stevia rebaudiana, SrKO (CYP701A5) and SrKAH (CYP81), in assays where substrate was supplemented to culture broth. With kaurene produced from glucose in the cell, SrCPR1 from S. rebaudiana supported highest turnover for KO-KAH combinations, besting two other CPRs isolated from S. rebaudiana, the Arabidopsis thaliana ATR2, and a new class I CPR12. Some coexpressions of ATR2 with a second CPR were found to diminish KAH activity, showing that coexpression of CPRs can lead to competition for CYPs with possibly adverse effects on catalysis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gold, Nicholas D.","Fossati, Elena","Hansen, Cecilie Ida Cetti","DiFalco, Marcos","Douchin, Veronique","Martin, Vincent J.J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-407075"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["diterpenoid biosynthesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a combinatorial approach to study cytochrome p000000000450 enzymes for de novo production of steviol glucosides in baker s yeast","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-407075","identifier":[{"id":"30474973","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85058527372","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-16d45d67-35b7-4a97-8553-b45b48385d36"],"keyword":["cytochrome P450 monooxygenase","cytochrome P450 reductase","diterpenoid biosynthesis","steviol glucosides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16C9D6F0F7831E6242A08399676CF98F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Nicholas D.","key":"goldpau","last":"Gold","name":"Gold, Nicholas D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elena","key":"fossatipau","last":"Fossati","name":"Fossati, Elena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie Ida Cetti","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"48c0d412-4ade-41c7-8ccc-ad9fde7ec352","name":"Hansen, Cecilie Ida Cetti","orcid":"0000-0002-0973-6466","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcos","key":"difalcopau","last":"DiFalco","name":"DiFalco, Marcos","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronique","key":"douchinpau","last":"Douchin","name":"Douchin, Veronique","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vincent J.J.","key":"martinpau","last":"Martin","name":"Martin, Vincent J.J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30474973"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acssynbio.8b00470","issn":["21615063"],"issue":"12","journal":"ACS Synthetic Biology","pages":"2918-2929","status":"p","title":"ACS Synthetic Biology","title_org":"A C S Synthetic Biology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058527372"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-16d45d67-35b7-4a97-8553-b45b48385d36"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Combinatorial Approach To Study Cytochrome P450 Enzymes for De Novo Production of Steviol Glucosides in Baker’s Yeast","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-407075","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Acid deposition arising from sulphur (S) and nitrogen (N) emissions from fossil fuel combustion and agriculture has contributed to the acidification of terrestrial ecosystems in many regions globally. However, in Europe and North America, S deposition has greatly decreased in recent decades due to emissions controls. In this study, we assessed the response of soil solution chemistry in mineral horizons of European forests to these changes. Trends in pH, acid neutralizing capacity (ANC), major ions, total aluminium (Altot) and dissolved organic carbon were determined for the period 1995–2012. Plots with at least 10 years of observations from the ICP Forests monitoring network were used. Trends were assessed for the upper mineral soil (10–20 cm, 104 plots) and subsoil (40–80 cm, 162 plots). There was a large decrease in the concentration of sulphate () in soil solution; over a 10‐year period (2000–2010), decreased by 52% at 10–20 cm and 40% at 40–80 cm. Nitrate was unchanged at 10–20 cm but decreased at 40–80 cm. The decrease in acid anions was accompanied by a large and significant decrease in the concentration of the nutrient base cations: calcium, magnesium and potassium (Bc = Ca2+ + Mg2+ + K+) and Altot over the entire dataset. The response of soil solution acidity was nonuniform. At 10–20 cm, ANC increased in acid‐sensitive soils (base saturation ≤10%) indicating a recovery, but ANC decreased in soils with base saturation >10%. At 40–80 cm, ANC remained unchanged in acid‐sensitive soils (base saturation ≤20%, ≤ 4.5) and decreased in better‐buffered soils (base saturation >20%, > 4.5). In addition, the molar ratio of Bc to Altot either did not change or decreased. The results suggest a long‐time lag between emission abatement and changes in soil solution acidity and underline the importance of long‐term monitoring in evaluating ecosystem response to decreases in deposition.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Johnson, James","Pannatier, Elisabeth Graf","Carnicelli, Stefano","Cecchini, Guia","Clarke, Nicholas","Cools, Nathalie","Hansen, Karin","Meesenburg, Henning","Nieminen, Tiina M.","Pihl‐Karlsson, Gunilla","Titeux, Hugues","Vanguelova, Elena","Verstraeten, Arne","Vesterdal, Lars","Waldner, Peter","Jonard, Mathieu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-519627"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Finland","Germany","Ireland","Italy","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Forestry Commission England","IVL - Swedish Environmental Research Institute","Natural Resources Institute Finland (Luke)","Northwest German Forest Research Institute","Norwegian Institute of Bioeconomy Research","Research Institute for Nature and Forest (INBO)","Research Institute for Nature and Forestry (INBO)","Swedish Environmental Protection Agency","Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research","University College Dublin","University of Florence","Université catholique de Louvain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the response of soil solution chemistry in european forests to decreasing acid deposition","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-519627","identifier":[{"id":"85046354689","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29604157","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d33625e4-757b-4f37-9fe1-28c7e9f2c622"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3AC447C99AD78B069D8DBDF54FB3B7BD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ie","key":"university college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"n