oi":"10.1038/s41467-018-04611-z","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"2252","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048556517"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d25ff1f7-455a-4c11-87ed-edec55141ef1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic inactivation of ANGPTL4 improves glucose homeostasis and is associated with reduced risk of diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-519128","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have identified >250 loci for body mass index (BMI), implicating pathways related to neuronal biology. Most GWAS loci represent clusters of common, noncoding variants from which pinpointing causal genes remains challenging. Here we combined data from 718,734 individuals to discover rare and low-frequency (minor allele frequency (MAF) < 5%) coding variants associated with BMI. We identified 14 coding variants in 13 genes, of which 8 variants were in genes (ZBTB7B, ACHE, RAPGEF3, RAB21, ZFHX3, ENTPD6, ZFR2 and ZNF169) newly implicated in human obesity, 2 variants were in genes (MC4R and KSR2) previously observed to be mutated in extreme obesity and 2 variants were in GIPR. The effect sizes of rare variants are ~10 times larger than those of common variants, with the largest effect observed in carriers of an MC4R mutation introducing a stop codon (p.Tyr35Ter, MAF = 0.01%), who weighed ~7 kg more than non-carriers. Pathway analyses based on the variants associated with BMI confirm enrichment of neuronal genes and provide new evidence for adipocyte and energy expenditure biology, widening the potential of genetically supported therapeutic targets in obesity.","author_count":75,"contributors":["Turcot, Valérie","Lu, Yingchang","Highland, Heather M","Schurmann, Claudia","Justice, Anne E","Fine, Rebecca S","Bradfield, Jonathan P","Esko, Tõnu","Giri, Ayush","Graff, Mariaelisa","Guo, Xiuqing","Hendricks, Audrey E","Karaderi, Tugce","Lempradl, Adelheid","Locke, Adam E","Mahajan, Anubha","Marouli, Eirini","Sivapalaratnam, Suthesh","Young, Kristin L","Alfred, Tamuno","Feitosa, Mary F","Masca, Nicholas G D","Manning, Alisa K","Medina-Gomez, Carolina","Mudgal, Poorva","Ng, Maggie C Y","Reiner, Alex P","Vedantam, Sailaja","Willems, Sara M","Winkler, Thomas W","Abecasis, Gonçalo","Aben, Katja K","Alam, Dewan S","Alharthi, Sameer E","Allison, Matthew","Amouyel, Philippe","Asselbergs, Folkert W","Auer, Paul L","Balkau, Beverley","Bang, Lia E","Barroso, Inês","Bastarache, Lisa","Benn, Marianne","Bergmann, Sven","Bielak, Lawrence F","Brandslund, Ivan","Christensen, Cramer","Jensen, Gorm B","Jørgensen, Marit Eika","Thuesen, Betina H","He, Liang"],"cuid":["S04-090.89-009878"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["CHD Exome+ Consortium","EPIC InterAct Consortium","EPIC-CVD Consortium","ExomeBP Consortium","Global Lipids Genetic Consortium","Global Lipids Genetics Consortium","GoT2D Genes Consortium","INTERVAL Study","MAGIC Investigators","ReproGen Consortium","T2D-Genes Consortium","The MAGIC Investigators","Understanding Society Scientific Group"],"country":["Canada","Cyprus","Estonia","France","Germany","Netherlands","Saudi Arabia","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Addenbrooke's Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Boston Children's Hospital","Broad Institute","Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Department of Biological Sciences, Faculty of Arts and Sciences, Eastern Mediterranean University, Famagusta, Cyprus.","Duke University","Erasmus University Medical Center","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Glenfield Hospital","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","King Abdulaziz University","Leipzig University","Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute","Max Planck Institute of Immunobiology and Epigenetics","Queen Mary University of London","Radboud University Medical Center","Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics","The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University College London","University of California","University of Cambridge","University of Colorado","University of Lille","University of Michigan","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Montreal","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hil