-3972","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 4 1 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonio","key":"zorzanoantoniopau","last":"Zorzano","name":"Zorzano, Antonio","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17 10 15 18","corresponding":null,"first":"Jose C","key":"florezjosecpau","last":"Florez","name":"Florez, Jose C","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 21","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorge","key":"ferrerjorgepau","last":"Ferrer","name":"Ferrer, Jorge","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16 1 10 15","corresponding":null,"first":"Josep Maria","key":"mercaderjosepmariapau","last":"Mercader","name":"Mercader, Josep Maria","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"27 1 28","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"torrentsdavidpau","last":"Torrents","name":"Torrents, David","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29358691"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-017-02380-9","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","pages":"321","paperid":"321","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041005929"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","danish diabetes academy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-281f70d5-2779-4090-b4f2-4579b8cd950f","au-ca988f0d-fd64-4b6c-8800-b08581ebdf0b","ku-7dc5909e-0823-44b2-a7c0-d841ebb2189f","sdu-0ed9f762-7d58-4d62-b962-4623e3ccae95"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Re-analysis of public genetic data reveals a rare X-chromosomal variant associated with type 2 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-002018","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Arctic marine ecosystems are threatened by new risks of Hg contamination under the combined effects of climate change and human activities. Rapid change of the cryosphere might for instance release large amounts of Hg trapped in sea-ice, permafrost and terrestrial glaciers over the last decades. Sea-ice disappearance is opening new shipping areas to polluting human industries. The general warming of ocean water masses is expected to affect the cycle of Hg, thereby increasing exposure of marine organisms. Hence, Hg could have high impacts on Arctic organisms, biodiversity and ecosystems and is still a source of major environmental concerns. In that context, providing a large-scale and comprehensive understanding of the Arctic marine food-web contamination is essential to better apprehend impacts of anthropogenic activities and climate change on the exposure of Arctic species and humans to Hg. In 2015, an international sampling network (ARCTOX) has been established, allowing the collection seabird samples all around the Arctic. Seabirds are indeed good indicators of Hg contamination of marine food webs at large spatial scale. Gathering researchers from 10 countries, ARCTOX allowed the collection of >5000 samples from twelve seabird species at >40 Arctic sites in 2015 and 2016. These different species have different trophic ecologies (diets and habitats) and will therefore provide information on Hg contamination for the different compartments of Arctic marine ecosystems (i.e benthic, pelagic, epontic, coastal, oceanic). By relying on this new network and by combining Hg analyses with biotelemetry, we aim at (1) monitoring spatio-temporal variations of Hg in Arctic biota. (2) Defining Arctic hotspots of Hg contamination and highlighting sensitive areas that require particular attention and protection. (3) Identifying non-Arctic sources of Hg contamination for migratory Arctic predators.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Fort, Jerome","Helgason, Halfdan","Amelineau, Francoise","Anker-Nilssen, Tycho","Bustnes, Jan Ove","Danielsen, Johannis","Dechamps, Sebastian","Dietz, Rune","Elliott, Kyle","Erikstad, Kjell Einar","Ezhov, Alexey","Gavrilo, Maria","Gilchrist, Grant","Gilg, Olivier","Grémillet, David","Hansen, Erpur S.","Hanssen, Sveinn Are","Helberg, Morten","Huffeldt, Nicholas Per","Jónsson, Jón Einar","Kitaysky, Alexander S.","Langseth, Magdalene","leclaire, sarah","Thórarinsson, Thorkell L.","Svein-Håkon, Lorentsen","Lorentzen, Erlend","Malleroy, Mark","Merkel, Flemming Ravn","Moe, Børge","Montevecchi, William A.","Mosbech, Anders","m.fl., [No Value]"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228785"],"event":{"end":"2018-07-21","place":"Providence, us","start":"2018-07-16","title":"13th International Conference on Mercury as a Global Pollutant (ICMGP2017)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Faroe Islands","France","Iceland","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carleton University","Faroe Marine Research Institute","French National Centre for Scientific Research (CNRS)","McGill University","Northeast Iceland Nature Research Centre","Norwegian Institute for Nature Research","South Iceland Nature Research Centre","University of Iceland","Université Bourgogne Europe"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"arctox a pan arctic sampling network to track mercury contamination across arctic marine food webs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://mercury2017.com/program/technical-program/1d-2/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228785","ids":