{"abstract":"Mobile location-based games are experiences that entertain its players by requiring interactions mainly at points of interest (POIs). Navigation between POIs often involve the use of either a physical or digital map, not taking advantage of the opportunity available to engage users in activities between POIs. The present paper examines, how riddle solving as a navigational method affects enjoyability, flow, and spatial presence.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nadarajah, Stephanie Githa","Overgaard, Benjamin Nicholas","Pedersen, Peder Walz","Schnatterbeck, Camilla Gisela Hansen","Rehm, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-062395"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-03","place":"Esbjerg, dk","start":"2016-05-02","title":"5th EAI International Conference: ArtsIT, Interactivity &amp; Game Creation","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Location based games","Smart city learning","flow experience artistic creativity flow theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enriching location based games with navigational game activities","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-062395","identifier":[{"id":"000425355100010","type":"wos"},{"id":"85015895126","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2aaae069-09da-48ad-bfbc-4ec61bad3419"],"keyword":["Location-based games","flow experience, artistic creativity, flow theory","smart city learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D54E55226A3CD6EA9FA3C1DB24820978"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":