2ab-7485-42f9-86bb-cfdd34c7db0e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparison of HapMap and 1000 Genomes Reference Panels in a Large-Scale Genome-Wide Association Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433032","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Modified atmosphere packing (MAP) is a technique to increase the shelf life of fresh meat. Continuing development of MAP requires better understanding of the physical and chemical processes taking place, in particular the diffusion of oxygen and its reaction with myoglobin. We model these processes using reaction-diffusion equations. The reactions include binding of oxygen to myoglobin, oxidation of myoglobin and other oxygen consuming processes. Model parameters have been extrapolated using data from the literature to relevant temperatures and pH values. Partial agreement with spatially resolved pigment concentration data is obtained, but only by substantially increasing the value of the oxygen consumption rate. Application of the model to meat stored at 5 °C shows that the metmyoglobin layer forms under the surface over a time scale of 24 h; The metmyoglobin layer forms deeper inside the meat proportional to the logarithm of the headspace oxygen partial pressure, thus improving the colour appearance of the meat.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tofteskov, Jon","Hansen, Jesper Schmidt","Bailey, Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-560118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autoxidation","Diffusion","Modelling","Myoglobin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling the autoxidation of myoglobin in fresh meat under modified atmosphere packing conditions","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-560118","identifier":[{"id":"85021781895","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-3d94c606-0f00-45c6-8e52-2bd390b9d4b1"],"keyword":["Autoxidation","Diffusion","Modelling","Myoglobin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24E65CDDB6F6D39431B0754CDBE60747"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Glass and Time"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"tofteskovpau","last":"Tofteskov","locid":"bc442e41-5742-45a1-828a-a92f528316ea","name":"Tofteskov, Jon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schmidt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"413f2c94-d35d-4ae4-89f2-361d8fc3ccc3","name":"Hansen, Jesper Schmidt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Nicholas","key":"baileypau","last":"Bailey","locid":"5dc0db10-4afc-4868-85f6-4872fbbc0686","name":"Bailey, Nicholas","orcid":"0000-0002-2519-2403","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jfoodeng.2017.06.002","issn":["02608774","18735770"],"issn_org":["02608774"],"journal":"Journal of Food Engineering","pages":"129-136","status":"p","title":"Journal of Food Engineering","volume":"214"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021781895"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-3d94c606-0f00-45c6-8e52-2bd390b9d4b1"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Modelling the autoxidation of myoglobin in fresh meat under modified atmosphere packing conditions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-560118","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"There are few examples of robust associations between rare copy number variants (CNVs) and complex continuous human traits. Here we present a large-scale CNV association meta-analysis on anthropometric traits in up to 191,161 adult samples from 26 cohorts. The study reveals five CNV associations at 1q21.1, 3q29, 7q11.23, 11p14.2, and 18q21.32 and confirms two known loci at 16p11.2 and 22q11.21, implicating at least one anthropometric trait. The discovered CNVs are recurrent and rare (0.01-0.2%), with large effects on height (>2.4 cm), weight (>5 kg), and body mass index (BMI) (>3.5 kg/m(2)). Burden analysis shows a 0.41 cm decrease in height, a 0.003 increase in waist-to-hip ratio and increase in BMI by 0.14 kg/m(2) for each Mb of total deletion burden (P = 2.5 × 10(-10), 6.0 × 10(-5), and 2.9 × 10(-3)). Our study provides evidence that the same genes (e.g., MC4R, FIBIN, and FMO5) harbor both common and rare variants affecting body size and that anthropometric traits share genetic loci with developmental and psychiatric disorders.Individual SNPs have small effects on anthropometric traits, yet the impact of CNVs has remained largely unknown. Here, Kutalik and co-workers perform a large-scale genome-wide meta-analysis of structural variation and find rare CNVs associated with height, weight and BMI with large effect sizes.","author_count":106,"contributors":["Macé, Aurélien","Tuke, Marcus A","Deelen, Patrick","Kristiansson, Kati","Mattsson, Hannele","Nõukas, Margit","Sapkota, Yadav","Schick, Ursula","Porcu, Eleonora","Rüeger, Sina","McDaid, Aaron F","Porteous, David","Winkler, Thomas W","Salvi, Erika","Shrine, Nick","Liu, Xueping","Ang, Wei Q","Zhang, Weihua","Feitosa, Mary F","Venturini, Cristina","van der Most, Peter J","Rosengren, Anders","Wood, Andrew R","Beaumont, Robin N","Jones, Samuel E","Ruth, Katherine S","Yaghootkar, Hanieh","Tyrrell, Jessica","Havulinna, Aki S","Boers, Harmen","Mägi, Reedik","Kriebel, Jennifer","Müller-Nurasyid, Martina","Perola, Markus","Nieminen, Markku","Lokki, Marja-Liisa","Kähönen, Mika","Viikari, Jorma S","Geller, Frank","Lahti, Jari","Palotie, Aarno","Koponen, Päivikki","Lundqvist, Annamari","Rissanen, Harri","Bottinger, Erwin P","Afaq, Saima","Wojczynski, Mary K","Lenzini, Petra","Nolte, Ilja M","Sparsø, Thomas","Schupf, Nicole","Christensen, Kaare","Perls, Thomas T","Newman, Anne B","Werge, Thomas","Snieder, Harold","Spector, Timothy D","Chambers, John C","Koskinen, Seppo","Melbye, Mads","Raitakari, Olli T","Lehtimäki, Terho","Tobin, Martin D","Wain, Louise V","Sinisalo, Juha","Peters, Annette","Meitinger, Thomas","Martin, Nicholas G","Wray, Naomi R","Montgomery, Grant W","Medland, Sarah E","Swertz, Morris A","Vartiainen, Erkki","Borodulin, Katja","Männistö, Satu","Murray, Anna","Bochud, Murielle","Jacquemont, Sébastien","Rivadeneira, Fernando","Hansen, Thomas F","Oldehinkel, Albertine J","Mangino, Massimo","Province, Michael A","Deloukas, Panos","Kooner, Jaspal S","Freathy, Rachel M","Pennell, Craig","Feenstra, Bjarke","Strachan, David P","Lettre, Guillaume","Hirschhorn, Joel","Cusi, Daniele","Heid, Iris M","Hayward, Caroline","Männik, Katrin","Beckmann, Jacques S","Loos, Ruth J F","Nyholt, Dale R","Metspalu, Andres","Eriksson, Johan G","Weedon, Michael N","Salomaa, Veikko","Franke, Lude","Reymond, Alexandre","Frayling, Timothy M","Kutalik, Zoltán"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045499"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Estonia","Finland","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Saudi Arabia","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston University School of Medicine","Columbia University","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Folkhälsan Research Center","German Center for Diabetes Research","Glenfield Hospital","