"","first":"Mark J.","key":"caulfieldmarkjpau","last":"Caulfield","name":"Caulfield, Mark J.","rank":136,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"elliottpaulpau","last":"Elliott","name":"Elliott, Paul","rank":137,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cecilia M.","key":"lindgrenceciliampau","last":"Lindgren","name":"Lindgren, Cecilia M.","rank":138,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"levydanielpau","last":"Levy","name":"Levy, Daniel","rank":139,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher","key":"newtonchehchristopherpau","last":"Newton-Cheh","name":"Newton-Cheh, Christopher","rank":140,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Patricia B.","key":"munroepatriciabpau","last":"Munroe","name":"Munroe, Patricia B.","rank":141,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Joanna M. M.","key":"howsonjoannammpau","last":"Howson","name":"Howson, Joanna M. M.","rank":142,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circgenetics.117.001778","issn":["1942325X","19423268"],"issn_org":["1942325X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Circulation: Cardiovascular Genetics","status":"p","title":"Circulation: Cardiovascular Genetics","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85032923056"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0641c703-261f-488e-9b8a-c7b5d6ea50f3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"New Blood Pressure-Associated Loci Identified in Meta-Analyses of 475000 Individuals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-397217","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"RUMD is a general purpose, high-performance molecular dynamics (MD) simulation package running on graphical processing units (GPU’s). RUMD addresses the challenge of utilizing the many-core nature of modern GPU hardware when simulating small to medium system sizes (roughly from a few thousand up to hundred thousand particles). It has a performance that is comparable to other GPU-MD codes at large system sizes and substantially better at smaller sizes. RUMD is open-source and consists of a library written in C++ and the CUDA extension to C, an easy-to-use Python interface, and a set of tools for set-up and post-simulation data analysis. The paper describes RUMD’s main features, optimizations and performance benchmarks.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bailey, Nicholas","Ingebrigtsen, Trond","Hansen, Jesper Schmidt","Veldhorst, Arno","Bøhling, Lasse","Lemarchand, Claire","Olsen, Andreas Elmerdahl","Bacher, Andreas Kvist","Costigliola, Lorenzo","Pedersen, Ulf Rørbæk","Larsen, Heine","Dyre, J. C.","Schrøder, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-559709"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rumd a general purpose molecular dynamics package optimized to utilize gpu hardware down to a few thousand particles","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21468/SciPostPhys.3.6.038","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-559709","identifier":[{"id":"85058333446","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-37a058da-5c38-4cb4-bdde-88520ab0b59d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-07490B73E4E08D12DADA7B2180046C0B"],"oa_link":[{"acc