3","issn":["00121797","1939327X"],"issn_org":["00121797"],"issue":"11","journal":"Diabetes","pages":"2888-2902","publisher":"American Diabetes Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Diabetes","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bc27dd82-ce45-4e74-a934-5ef0ac509e8e","ku-186f9856-9b4a-4825-b7dd-9300b4c708b2","sdu-fee6deae-87f9-4766-83d8-11c0f3a793aa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"An Expanded Genome-Wide Association Study of Type 2 Diabetes in Europeans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-088.64-009075","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Extensive tissue remodeling mediated by matrix metalloproteases (MMPs) is an important part of cancer. The aim of this study was to investigate whether serum biomarkers reflecting MMP-mediated degradation of type I collagen (C1M), type IV collagen (C4M) and citrullinated vimentin (VICM) were predictive of cancer-specific mortality. Between 1999 and 2001, 5855 Danish postmenopausal women participated in The Prospective Epidemiologic Risk Factor (PERF I) study. Demographics and serum samples were collected at enrolment. Cancer diagnosis, and cause and time of death were obtained from Danish registries. C1M, C4M and VICM were measured by ELISA. Hazard ratios (HR) and Kaplan-Meier curves were applied to assess mortality at 3 and 12 years of follow-up for women diagnosed with cancer within 3 years from blood sampling. Within 3 years from blood sampling, 250 women had been diagnosed with cancer. C1M and VICM were associated with survival over time at 3 years of follow-up. Only C1M was predictive of mortality at 3 years follow-up: the adjusted HR was 2.65 [95% CI: 1.08-6.51]. In conclusion, C1M and VICM are associated with survival in postmenopausal women with cancer, and C1M is an independent risk factor for cancer-specific mortality. Thus, quantification of tissue remodeling is important in cancer.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Willumsen, Nicholas","Bager, Cecilie L","Kehlet, Stephanie N.","Dragsbæk, Katrine","Neergaard, Jesper S","Hansen, Henrik Bo","Bay-Jensen, Anne-Christine","Leeming, Diana Julie","Lipton, Allan","Christiansen, Claus","Karsdal, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-599947"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Penn State Health Milton S. Hershey Medical Center","The Pennsylvania State University"],"keyword":["Cancer","ECM","MMP","Mortality","type I collagen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NBIO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"excessive matrix metalloprotease mediated degradation of interstitial tissue type i collagen independently predicts short term survival in an observational study of postmenopausal women diagnosed with cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.15275","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-599947","identifier":[{"id":"85039741387","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28698394","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-5d721951-d371-4b45-b148-e4d62b8d07ad"],"keyword":["ECM","MMP","cancer","mortality","type I collagen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D3681869EE960AB6B8AEEFAE840E7A26"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/135405657/Excessive_matrix_metalloprotease_mediated_degradation_of_interstitial_tissue_type_I_collagen_independently_predicts_short_term_survival_in_an_observational_study_of_postmenopausal_women_diagnosed_with_cancer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.15275","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"the pennsylvania state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"The Pennsylvania State University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"penn state health milton s hershey medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Penn State Health Milton S. Hershey Medical Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas","key":"willumsenpau","last":"Willumsen","locid":"7d600d16-667c-4b12-9fc9-012618200ac0","name":"Willumsen, Nicholas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie L","key":"bagerpau","last":"Bager","name":"Bager, Cecilie L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephanie N.","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","name":"Kehlet, Stephanie N.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"dragsbækpau","last":"Dragsbæk","name":"Dragsbæk, Katrine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper S","key":"neergaardpau","last":"Neergaard","name":"Neergaard, Jesper S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bo","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Bo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Christine","key":"bayjensenpau","last":"Bay-Jensen","name":"Bay-Jensen, Anne-Christine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Diana Julie","key":"leemingpau","last":"Leeming","name":"Leeming, Diana Julie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"liptonpau","last":"Lipton","name":"Lipton, Allan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Claus","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"karsdalpau","last":"Karsdal","name":"Karsdal, Morten","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28698394"],"pub":{"doi":"10.18632/oncotarget.15275","issn":["19492553"],"issue":"32","journal":"OncoTarget","pages":"52501-52510","publisher":"Impact Journals LLC","status":"p","title":"OncoTarget","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039741387"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Nordic Bioscience","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5d721951-d371-4b45-b148-e4d62b8d07ad"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Excessive matrix metalloprotease-mediated degradation of interstitial tissue (type I collagen) independently predicts short-term survival in an observational study of postmenopausal women diagnosed with cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-599947","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Location-based games entertain players usually by interactions at points of interest (POIs). Navigation between POIs often involve the use of either a physical or digital map, not taking advantage of the opportunity available to engage users in activities between POIs. The paper presents riddle solving as a navigational method for a location-based game. 10 families with 2-6 persons and at least one child in the age range 9-11 years old participated in the evaluation. Results show that riddle solving as a navigational method is more enjoyable than a 2D digital map. Additional findings from video recordings, field notes, questionnaires, logging and semi-structured interviews revealed that riddle solving has potential for engaging users in learning activities.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nadarajah, Stephanie Githa","Overgaard, Benjamin Nicholas","Pedersen, Peder Walz","Schnatterbeck, Camilla Gisela Hansen","Rehm, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056541"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gamification","Location based interaction","Navigation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gamifying navigation in location based applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4108/eai.8-11-2017.153333","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-056541","ids":["aau-1617aaa5-f55d-47f8-acc2-886b8e98b336"],"keyword":["Gamification","Location-based interaction","Navigation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D33FC86400217C9F2C1CA64AC3BB06E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4108/eai.8-11-2017.153333","version