,"rank":316,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L Adrienne","key":"cupplesladriennepau","last":"Cupples","name":"Cupples, L Adrienne","rank":317,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28443625"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms14977","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"14977","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019322396"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-52ae0d5b-8b57-4320-b771-4af04148e46e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genome-wide meta-analysis of 241,258 adults accounting for smoking behaviour identifies novel loci for obesity traits","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-442792","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Statin treatment and variants in the gene encoding HMG-CoA reductase are associated with reductions in both the concentration of LDL cholesterol and the risk of coronary heart disease, but also with modest hyperglycaemia, increased bodyweight, and modestly increased risk of type 2 diabetes, which in no way offsets their substantial benefits. We sought to investigate the associations of LDL cholesterol-lowering PCSK9 variants with type 2 diabetes and related biomarkers to gauge the likely effects of PCSK9 inhibitors on diabetes risk. METHODS: In this mendelian randomisation study, we used data from cohort studies, randomised controlled trials, case control studies, and genetic consortia to estimate associations of PCSK9 genetic variants with LDL cholesterol, fasting blood glucose, HbA1c, fasting insulin, bodyweight, waist-to-hip ratio, BMI, and risk of type 2 diabetes, using a standardised analysis plan, meta-analyses, and weighted gene-centric scores. FINDINGS: Data were available for more than 550 000 individuals and 51 623 cases of type 2 diabetes. Combined analyses of four independent PCSK9 variants (rs11583680, rs11591147, rs2479409, and rs11206510) scaled to 1 mmol/L lower LDL cholesterol showed associations with increased fasting glucose (0·09 mmol/L, 95% CI 0·02 to 0·15), bodyweight (1·03 kg, 0·24 to 1·82), waist-to-hip ratio (0·006, 0·003 to 0·010), and an odds ratio for type diabetes of 1·29 (1·11 to 1·50). Based on the collected data, we did not identify associations with HbA1c (0·03%, -0·01 to 0·08), fasting insulin (0·00%, -0·06 to 0·07), and BMI (0·11 kg/m(2), -0·09 to 0·30). INTERPRETATION: PCSK9 variants associated with lower LDL cholesterol were also associated with circulating higher fasting glucose concentration, bodyweight, and waist-to-hip ratio, and an increased risk of type 2 diabetes. In trials of PCSK9 inhibitor drugs, investigators should carefully assess these safety outcomes and quantify the risks and benefits of PCSK9 inhibitor treatment, as was previously done for statins. FUNDING: British Heart Foundation, and University College London Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust (UCLH) National Institute for Health Research (NIHR) Biomedical Research Centre.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Schmidt, Amand F","Swerdlow, Daniel I","Holmes, Michael V","Patel, Riyaz S","Fairhurst-Hunter, Zammy","Lyall, Donald M","Hartwig, Fernando Pires","Horta, Bernardo Lessa","Hyppönen, Elina","Power, Christine","Moldovan, Max","van Iperen, Erik","Hovingh, G Kees","Demuth, Ilja","Norman, Kristina","Steinhagen-Thiessen, Elisabeth","Demuth, Juri","Bertram, Lars","Liu, Tian","Coassin, Stefan","Willeit, Johann","Kiechl, Stefan","Willeit, Karin","Mason, Dan","Wright, John","Morris, Richard","Wanamethee, Goya","Whincup, Peter","Ben-Shlomo, Yoav","McLachlan, Stela","Price, Jackie F","Kivimaki, Mika","Welch, Catherine","Sanchez-Galvez, Adelaida","Marques-Vidal, Pedro","Nicolaides, Andrew","Panayiotou, Andrie G","Onland-Moret, N Charlotte","van der Schouw, Yvonne T","Matullo, Giuseppe","Fiorito, Giovanni","Guarrera, Simonetta","Sacerdote, Carlotta","Wareham, Nicholas J","Langenberg, Claudia","Scott, Robert","Grarup, Niels","Pedersen, Oluf","Hansen, Torben","Linneberg, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543275"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["LifeLines Cohort study group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i pcsk000000000009 i genetic variants and risk of type 000000000002 diabetes a mendelian randomisation study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2213-8587(16)30396-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-543275","identifier":[{"id":"27908689","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85007330927","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5266795","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-fb030f45-4bfe-4795-9130-969aaa64ef88"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3829884F0EA2DA59B815010D2D28D28B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/183506117/1_s2.0_S2213858716303965_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2213-8587(16)30396-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Grarup Group","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and Metagenomics in Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"lifelines cohort study group","name":"LifeLines Cohort study group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Amand F","key":"schmidtamandfpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Amand F","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel I","key":"swerdlowdanielipau","last":"Swerdlow","name":"Swerdlow, Daniel I","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael V","key":"holmesmichaelvpau","last":"Holmes","name":"Holmes, Michael V","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Riyaz S","key":"patelriyazspa