{"abstract":"We present a theoretical framework by which virtual world sound designers may work towards the attainment of presence. Drawing on the study of cognitive metaphors and the view that sound is an emergent perception we offer an account of the environment as a salient and dynamic construct that functions as a synecdoche for the nonself. Separating environment from world, we discuss the role of sound in the forming of the environment and argue that it is this environment that establishes the means for presence because it is the process behind the construction of the environment that individuates self from nonself and such differentiation is a defining feature of the concept of presence.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Walther-Hansen, Mads","Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-104397"],"event":{"acronym":"Audiomostly","end":"2016-10-06","place":"Norrköping, se","start":"2016-10-04","title":"11th Audio Mostly Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Crossmodality","Embodiment","Environment","Metaphor","Presence","Sound","Virtual worlds"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"being in a virtual world presence environment salience sound","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2986425","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-104397","identifier":[{"id":"000390600700011","type":"wos"},{"id":"84999115125","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bb57bd99-79a7-436e-b044-d08bafd4982a"],"keyword":["Crossmodality","Embodiment","Environment","Metaphor","Presence","Sound","Virtual worlds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F9BEDF94B8A754D085D4A7DFD0358C20"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music & Sound Knowledge Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"waltherhansenpau","last":"Walther-Hansen","locid":"73804945-3d74-4f54-a2db-ab1be9009c09","name":"Walther-Hansen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0001-5746-5093","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"grimshawpau","last":"Grimshaw","locid":"673322d2-f25b-4f45-93b2-ba1c4c9fdbc5","name":"Grimshaw-Aagaard, Mark Nicholas","name_org":"Grimshaw, Mark","orcid":"0000-0003-0485-6087","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2986416.2986425","eisbn":["9781450348225"],"pages":"77-84","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","subtitle":"A Conference on Interaction With Sound","title":"Proceedings of the 11th Audio Mostly Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84999115125"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bb57bd99-79a7-436e-b044-d08bafd4982a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Being in a Virtual World : Presence, Environment, Salience, Sound","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-104397","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
