{"abstract":"The global burden of atrial fibrillation and diabetes mellitus (diabetes) is considerable, and prevalence rates are increasing. Diabetes is associated with an increased risk of developing atrial fibrillation; however, diabetes also influences the management and prognosis of atrial fibrillation. In the following article, the authors describe the association between diabetes and atrial fibrillation; specifically, the significance of diabetes on the risk of atrial fibrillation, ischemic stroke and bleeding complications associated with anticoagulation. In addition, the authors evaluate the risks and outcomes of heart failure and the success rates of both ablation and cardioversion in atrial fibrillation patients with diabetes. Finally, this article describes the association of HbA1c levels with the management and prognosis of atrial fibrillation patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pallisgaard, Jannik Langtved","Lindhardt, Tommi Bo","Olesen, Jonas Bjerring","Hansen, Morten Lock","Carlson, Nicholas","Gislason, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-042487"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Ablation","Anticoagulants","Atrial fibrillation","Bleeding","Cardioversion","Cost of Illness","Diabetes Complications","Diabetes mellitus","HbA1c","Heart failure","Hemoglobin A Glycosylated","Hemorrhage","Humans","Prevalence","Prognosis","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"management and prognosis of atrial fibrillation in the diabetic patient","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84929899537","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["JL Pallisgaard, TB Lindhardt, JB Olesen and ML Hansen participated in a study funded by an unrestricted research grant from Boehringer-Ingel-heim. GH Gislason is supported by an unrestricted clinical research scholarship from the Novo Nordisk Foundation and Boehringer-Ingelheim. The authors have no other relevant affiliations or financial involvement with any organization or entity with a financial interest in or financial conflict with the subject matter or materials discussed in the manuscript apart from those disclosed."],"id":"S02-100.00-042487","identifier":[{"id":"84929899537","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26000562","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-546e23f3-8339-4d68-a2ef-93664b2bf795","sdu-d570f805-2aa7-488e-9c54-ab26576f961c"],"keyword":["Anticoagulants","Atrial Fibrillation","Cost of Illness","Diabetes Complications","Diabetes Mellitus","HbA1c","Hemoglobin A, Glycosylated","Hemorrhage","Humans","Prevalence","Prognosis","Stroke","ablation","bleeding","cardioversion","heart failure","novel oral anticoagulants"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AA41359615D28AFA5A0BC22851AC3229"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","name