 Dora","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa","key":"noratpau","last":"Norat","name":"Norat, Teresa","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elio","key":"ribolipau","last":"Riboli","name":"Riboli, Elio","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rudolf","key":"kaakspau","last":"Kaaks","name":"Kaaks, Rudolf","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23492765"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/aje/kws309","issn":["00029262","14766256"],"issn_org":["00029262"],"issue":"8","journal":"American Journal of Epidemiology","pages":"787-99","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"177"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ee3e95ba-1a77-4f23-93e0-9c64c09b0f7d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hormonal, Metabolic, and Inflammatory Profiles and Endometrial Cancer Risk Within the EPIC Cohort : A Factor Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-265295","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The combination of ataxia and hypogonadism was first described more than a century ago, but its genetic basis has remained elusive. METHODS We performed whole-exome sequencing in a patient with ataxia and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, followed by targeted sequencing of candidate genes in similarly affected patients. Neurologic and reproductive endocrine phenotypes were characterized in detail. The effects of sequence variants and the presence of an epistatic interaction were tested in a zebrafish model. RESULTS Digenic homozygous mutations in RNF216 and OTUD4, which encode a ubiquitin E3 ligase and a deubiquitinase, respectively, were found in three affected siblings in a consanguineous family. Additional screening identified compound heterozygous truncating mutations in RNF216 in an unrelated patient and single heterozygous deleterious mutations in four other patients. Knockdown of rnf216 or otud4 in zebrafish embryos induced defects in the eye, optic tectum, and cerebellum; combinatorial suppression of both genes exacerbated these phenotypes, which were rescued by nonmutant, but not mutant, human RNF216 or OTUD4 messenger RNA. All patients had progressive ataxia and dementia. Neuronal loss was observed in cerebellar pathways and the hippocampus; surviving hippocampal neurons contained ubiquitin-immunoreactive intranuclear inclusions. Defects were detected at the hypothalamic and pituitary levels of the reproductive endocrine axis. CONCLUSIONS The syndrome of hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, ataxia, and dementia can be caused by inactivating mutations in RNF216 or by the combination of mutations in RNF216 and OTUD4. These findings link disordered ubiquitination to neurodegeneration and reproductive dysfunction and highlight the power of whole-exome sequencing in combination with functional studies to unveil genetic interactions that cause disease.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Margolin, David H.","Kousi, Maria","Chan, Yee-Ming","Lim, Elaine T.","Schmahmann, Jeremy D.","Hadjivassiliou, Marios","Hall, Janet E.","Adam, Ibrahim","Dwyer, Andrew","Plummer, Lacey","Aldrin, Stephanie V.","O'Rourke, Julia","Kirby, Andrew","Hansen, Kasper Lage","Milunsky, Aubrey","Milunsky, Jeff M.","Chan, Jennifer","Hedley-Whyte, E. Tessa","Daly, Mark J.","Katsanis, Nicholas","Seminara, Stephanie B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-323496"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ataxia dementia and hypogonadotropism caused by disordered ubiquitination","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa1215993","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-323496","identifier":[{"id":"84877935385","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3f93478d-1e96-4fe9-9f20-83e75613d523"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8C8CE0A98D10996437C9CE5FC26B87D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa1215993","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis, Integrat