{"abstract":"Circulating levels of adiponectin, a hormone produced predominantly by adipocytes, are highly heritable and are inversely associated with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2D) and other metabolic traits. We conducted a meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies in 39,883 individuals of European ancestry to identify genes associated with metabolic disease. We identified 8 novel loci associated with adiponectin levels and confirmed 2 previously reported loci (P = 4.5×10(-8)-1.2×10(-43)). Using a novel method to combine data across ethnicities (N = 4,232 African Americans, N = 1,776 Asians, and N = 29,347 Europeans), we identified two additional novel loci. Expression analyses of 436 human adipocyte samples revealed that mRNA levels of 18 genes at candidate regions were associated with adiponectin concentrations after accounting for multiple testing (p","author_count":55,"contributors":["Dastani, Zari","Hivert, Marie-France","Timpson, Nicholas","Perry, John R B","Yuan, Xin","Scott, Robert A","Henneman, Peter","Heid, Iris M","Kizer, Jorge R","Lyytikäinen, Leo-Pekka","Fuchsberger, Christian","Tanaka, Toshiko","Morris, Andrew P","Small, Kerrin","Isaacs, Aaron","Beekman, Marian","Coassin, Stefan","Lohman, Kurt","Qi, Lu","Kanoni, Stavroula","Pankow, James S","Uh, Hae-Won","Wu, Ying","Bidulescu, Aurelian","Rasmussen-Torvik, Laura J","Greenwood, Celia M T","Ladouceur, Martin","Grimsby, Jonna","Manning, Alisa K","Liu, Ching-Ti","Kooner, Jaspal","Mooser, Vincent E","Vollenweider, Peter","Kapur, Karen A","Chambers, John","Wareham, Nicholas J","Langenberg, Claudia","Frants, Rune","Willems-Vandijk, Ko","Oostra, Ben A","Willems, Sara M","Lamina, Claudia","Winkler, Thomas W","Grarup, Niels","Jørgensen, Torben","Sparsø, Thomas Hempel","Hansen, Torben","Pedersen, Oluf","Karpe, Fredrik","Kyvik, Kirsten Ohm"],"cuid":["S03-089.13-028809"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["DIAGRAM+ Consortium","GLGC Consortium","MAGIC Consortium"],"keyword":["Adiponectin","African Americans","Asian Continental Ancestry Group","Cholesterol HDL","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","European Continental Ancestry Group","Female","Gene expression","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Insulin Resistance","Male","Metabolic Networks and Pathways","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Waist Hip Ratio"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel loci for adiponectin levels and their influence on type 000000000002 diabetes and metabolic traits a multi ethnic meta analysis of 000000000045 000000000891 individuals","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1002607","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-089.13-028809","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3315470","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84859238629","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22479202","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-de93aa13-977e-425a-b449-40168dac3462","ku-bd32e392-8527-49ff-8cd7-3d6a32652ae5","sdu-fb7da986-aea9-4d20-89a9-e02b71bf04e4"],"keyword":["Adiponectin","African Americans","Asian Continental Ancestry Group","Cholesterol, HDL","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","European Continental Ancestry Group","Female","Gene Expression","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome-Wide Association Study","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Insulin Resistance","Male","Metabolic Networks and Pathways","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Waist-Hip Ratio"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-983DD4AEB19B76EA81E3087E122DCDF9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/jou